{"type":"text","timestamp":1791394349764,"sessionID":"ses_ee89c2ab9ffergyxR5ZG3Tj4o0","part":{"id":"prt_1176c77b0001PD4QPAELOrWmtv","messageID":"msg_1176c5f65001pOQEarHt8RmOVn","sessionID":"ses_ee89c2ab9ffergyxR5ZG3Tj4o0","type":"text","text":"Job completed. Here's a summary of what I did and found.\n\n## Context\n\nI was resuming the `cover` job on branch `feature/cover_reload-after-time-away` (verified it matches `brief.md`). A prior session had left most of the implementation uncommitted in the worktree but never finished, verified, or committed it. I reviewed that work, completed the missing pieces, verified, and committed.\n\n## What was implemented (TASK-1 … TASK-7)\n\n- **TASK-1 — shared session token.** All 33 state stores now use `auth.apiService` instead of snapshotting `auth.getToken()` at construction, and `Auth.clear()` wipes the token on the shared instance.\n- **TASK-2 — resume re-validation.** `Auth` revalidates on `visibilitychange`→visible, `online`, and an hourly interval while visible (browser-guarded); near/expired token triggers a single-flight `refresh()` then `loadAdditionalData()`; definitive rejection logs out.\n- **TASK-3 — global 401 recovery.** `ApiService.fetchWithRecovery()` runs a single-retry recovery ladder (adopt another tab's persisted token → refresh → last-resort logout), bypasses auth endpoints, and never triggers on network errors.\n- **TASK-4 — surface failed note mutations.** `Notes.create()`/`createCategory()` now emit a translation-aware `UiNotifications.error()` and keep the modal + input on failure. I also had to stop `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` from closing the modal optimistically (the store now closes on success) — documented as a necessary deviation from the task's file list.\n- **TASK-5 — reactive logout guard.** Root `+layout.svelte` `$effect` redirects to login/setup with a session-expired notice on a mid-session logout transition.\n- **TASK-6 — profile-image audit.** Concluded the earlier fix (service-worker same-origin guard + `NavProfileEntry` retry/fallback) is **not** redundant: it covers a broken in-session image fetch, while the resume work covers stale data. Kept everything; no code change.\n- **TASK-7 — verification.** `npm run check` = 0 errors/0 warnings; `npm test` = 715 passed (1 pre-existing, unrelated `StatisticWidget` component-test failure); ESLint clean on changed files. `prettier --check` fails repo-wide (402 files, including untouched `HEAD` versions) — pre-existing drift, not from this job. No backend was available (`localhost:8000` refused), so the two backend token-TTL facts remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately agnostic and manual simulation steps are documented.\n\n## Notable follow-ups (in `implementation.md`)\n\n- 8 components still build their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())` (outside TASK-1's `state/*` scope) and can still go stale.\n- `NavProfileEntry.failed` only resets when the image path changes.\n- Pre-existing repo-wide prettier drift and the unrelated component-test failure.\n\n## Commits\n\n- `7725ae4` — all source + test changes\n- `8a28a87` — `implementation.md` summary\n- `69bcda8`, `f2669e4` — session-log sync\n\nThe only thing not clean at the end is `session.log`, which is the harness's live per-tool-call log — every commit appends to it after the fact, so it can never converge to clean from inside the session.","time":{"start":1791394346928,"end":1791394349757}}}
