{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791394510116,"sessionID":"ses_ee8912192ffeUaFB6dscdlJxUU","part":{"id":"prt_1176ef520001c35UPR1XVBopRJ","messageID":"msg_1176ef0d3001maBicts6m7pQnX","sessionID":"ses_ee8912192ffeUaFB6dscdlJxUU","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394511355,"sessionID":"ses_ee8912192ffeUaFB6dscdlJxUU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_h17FxQbFsad3vPocYxu35306","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: reload after time away\n2: \n3: id: cover\n4: status: open\n5: analyst:\n6: date: 2026-08-19\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Diagnosis\n11: \n12: The session is validated exactly once, at app boot:\n13: \n14: - `Auth` (constructor → `load()`) checks `authToken.expires_at`, refreshes only if\n15:   within 5 days (web) / 14 days (native), then fetches `/users/me`. Nothing ever\n16:   re-runs this while the app stays open — no timer, no `visibilitychange` hook.\n17: - Every feature store snapshots the token at construction\n18:   (`new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`), and `Auth.refresh()` only updates\n19:   Auth's own `ApiService` instance. A refreshed token never reaches the stores.\n20: - `ApiService` swallows every non-ok response (`res.ok ? … : null/false`): no 401\n21:   handling, no retry, no logout, no user feedback.\n22: \n23: So a permanently-open tab drifts into a zombie state: `loggedIn === true` in\n24: memory, token expired/invalid → all API calls fail silently (`Notes.create()`\n25: returns `null` and the modal just closes — \"nothing happens\"; user data incl.\n26: `profile.profile_image_path` is never re-fetched). A hard reload re-runs\n27: `Auth.load()` (expiry check → refresh → `loadAdditionalData()`), which is why\n28: reloading fixes everything.\n29: \n30: The earlier profile-image fix (re-fetching `/users/me` via `loadAdditionalData()`\n31: + `save()`) most likely addressed a symptom of this same root cause; with a\n32: proper resume-driven session check it is probably redundant — audited in TASK-6.\n33: \n34: Out of scope: service worker changes (it already skips API calls), backend\n35: token TTL changes, refactoring all stores to a shared ApiService beyond what\n36: token propagation requires.\n37: \n38: ## Task breakdown\n39: \n40: TASK-1 (decided: Option B): Share Auth's `ApiService` instance across stores.\n41: `Auth` already owns an `ApiService` and keeps its token current on\n42: login/refresh; replace each store's `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`\n43: with `this.auth.apiService` (one mechanical line per store) so a runtime\n44: refresh reaches every request automatically. `logout()` must clear the token on\n45: that shared instance so no store keeps sending the old token. Do not touch\n46: unrelated store logic.\n47: files: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, plus the one-line constructor change in\n48: src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts (~36 stores)\n49: depends: none\n50: risk: medium — every API call now goes through one shared instance; the change\n51: is mechanical per store and covered by `npm run check`.\n52: \n53: TASK-2: Re-validate the session when the app is used again after time away:\n54: on `visibilitychange` → visible (and `online`), plus a low-frequency interval\n55: while visible (e.g. hourly), check `expires_at` — expired → logout; within\n56: refresh threshold → `refresh()` (single-flight: never two concurrent refreshes);\n57: then `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user incl. profile image\n58: path. Guard all listener registration with `browser` (no SSR access to\n59: `document`). Follow the existing `UserNotifications` pattern\n60: (`visibilitychange` + interval, interval stopped while hidden). The routine\n61: check is a local date comparison — no network unless action is needed.\n62: files: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts\n63: depends: TASK-1\n64: risk: medium — new lifecycle listeners and async races; must not double-refresh,\n65: must behave sanely on the desktop/mobile shells (app resume vs. tab visibility).\n66: \n67: TASK-3: Global 401 recovery in `ApiService` — logout strictly as the last\n68: resort. On a 401 from a non-auth endpoint, run a recovery ladder:\n69: (a) re-read the persisted auth from localStorage — if another tab refreshed\n70: the token (multi-tab staleness), adopt it and retry the request (covers\n71: \"stale token although user is still authed\"); (b) otherwise single-flight\n72: `refresh()` and retry the original request exactly once with the new token;\n73: (c) only log out (with UI notification + redirect via TASK-5) if the refresh\n74: itself fails with a definitive auth rejection. Network errors (fetch\n75: rejection / offline) must NOT log out — they are transient and Layer 2\n76: re-checks on `online`. Must explicitly bypass the auth endpoints\n77: (`auth.login`, `auth.refresh`, forgot/reset password, passkey authenticate) —\n78: a failed login legitimately returns 401 and must not trigger recovery. Never\n79: retry a request more than once. New user-visible strings must be added to all\n80: four i18n files.\n81: files: src/lib/services/ApiService.ts, src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts,\n82: src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n83: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n84: risk: high — retry-on-401 logic can loop or misfire; several endpoints return\n85: 401 for normal reasons; `postRaw` parses error bodies and needs care.\n86: \n87: TASK-4: Stop swallowing failed mutations for the reported symptom: surface\n88: `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures via `UiNotifications.error()`\n89: (translation-aware), keeping the user's input in the modal instead of\n90: discarding it. Do not refactor other stores in this job.\n91: files: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts,\n92: src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n93: depends: TASK-3 (so 401s are recovered rather than toasted twice)\n94: risk: low — small, local change; i18n sync is enforced by `npm run check`.\n95: \n96: TASK-5: Make the root layout react to a mid-session logout: the auth guard in\n97: `+layout.svelte` only runs in `onMount`, so `loggedIn` flipping to false after\n98: TASK-2/TASK-3 leaves the user on a dead page. Add a reactive guard (e.g.\n99: `$effect` on `auth.loggedIn`) that redirects to login, without fighting the\n100: existing onMount guard or triggering on auth/setup routes.\n101: files: src/routes/+layout.svelte\n102: depends: TASK-2, TASK-3\n103: risk: low-medium — navigation side effects; must not redirect-loop.\n104: \n105: TASK-6: Audit the previous profile-image fix for redundancy: with resume-driven\n106: `loadAdditionalData()` in place, check whether the earlier change (re-fetch of\n107: `/users/me` after login/`load()`, `profileCache`) still guards a distinct\n108: scenario (e.g. image re-upload changing the storage path, cache busting) and\n109: keep or remove it with a written justification in implementation.md.\n110: files: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte,\n111: src/routes/profile/+page.svelte\n112: depends: TASK-2\n113: risk: low-medium — removing it without confirming the covered scenario could\n114: re-break the profile image.\n115: \n116: TASK-7: Verify: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`; manually simulate\n117: the stale session (dev API with short token TTL or hand-edited `auth` localStorage\n118: entry: (a) expired token + resume from background → refreshed-and-recovered if\n119: the backend honors a grace window, otherwise clean logout — determine which;\n120: (b) near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, notes create works; (c) invalid\n121: token server-side → 401 recovery ladder incl. localStorage adoption for the\n122: multi-tab case; (d) offline/fetch-rejection → no logout, transient only).\n123: Deduced from the client (single bearer token, refresh authenticates with the\n124: current token, empty body): the two open backend facts — (1) does refresh\n125: accept an already-expired token, (2) is the old token revoked on rotation —\n126: are to be probed empirically (curl dev API) and recorded here; the\n127: implementation is deliberately agnostic to both (see recovery ladder), they\n128: only pin down expected outcomes for (a) and (c). Document steps/results in\n129: implementation.md.\n130: files: docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md\n131: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6\n132: risk: low — verification only; no component-test infra exists, so manual steps\n133: are required.\n\n(End of file - total 133 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-08-19\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe session is validated exactly once, at app boot:\n\n- `Auth` (constructor → `load()`) checks `authToken.expires_at`, refreshes only if\n  within 5 days (web) / 14 days (native), then fetches `/users/me`. Nothing ever\n  re-runs this while the app stays open — no timer, no `visibilitychange` hook.\n- Every feature store snapshots the token at construction\n  (`new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`), and `Auth.refresh()` only updates\n  Auth's own `ApiService` instance. A refreshed token never reaches the stores.\n- `ApiService` swallows every non-ok response (`res.ok ? … : null/false`): no 401","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-08-19\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe session is validated exactly once, at app boot:\n\n- `Auth` (constructor → `load()`) checks `authToken.expires_at`, refreshes only if\n  within 5 days (web) / 14 days (native), then fetches `/users/me`. Nothing ever\n  re-runs this while the app stays open — no timer, no `visibilitychange` hook.\n- Every feature store snapshots the token at construction\n  (`new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`), and `Auth.refresh()` only updates\n  Auth's own `ApiService` instance. A refreshed token never reaches the stores.\n- `ApiService` swallows every non-ok response (`res.ok ? … : null/false`): no 401\n  handling, no retry, no logout, no user feedback.\n\nSo a permanently-open tab drifts into a zombie state: `loggedIn === true` in\nmemory, token expired/invalid → all API calls fail silently (`Notes.create()`\nreturns `null` and the modal just closes — \"nothing happens\"; user data incl.\n`profile.profile_image_path` is never re-fetched). A hard reload re-runs\n`Auth.load()` (expiry check → refresh → `loadAdditionalData()`), which is why\nreloading fixes everything.\n\nThe earlier profile-image fix (re-fetching `/users/me` via `loadAdditionalData()`\n+ `save()`) most likely addressed a symptom of this same root cause; with a\nproper resume-driven session check it is probably redundant — audited in TASK-6.\n\nOut of scope: service worker changes (it already skips API calls), backend\ntoken TTL changes, refactoring all stores to a shared ApiService beyond what\ntoken propagation requires.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1 (decided: Option B): Share Auth's `ApiService` instance across stores.\n`Auth` already owns an `ApiService` and keeps its token current on\nlogin/refresh; replace each store's `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`\nwith `this.auth.apiService` (one mechanical line per store) so a runtime\nrefresh reaches every request automatically. `logout()` must clear the token on\nthat shared instance so no store keeps sending the old token. Do not touch\nunrelated store logic.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, plus the one-line constructor change in\nsrc/lib/state/*.svelte.ts (~36 stores)\ndepends: none\nrisk: medium — every API call now goes through one shared instance; the change\nis mechanical per store and covered by `npm run check`.\n\nTASK-2: Re-validate the session when the app is used again after time away:\non `visibilitychange` → visible (and `online`), plus a low-frequency interval\nwhile visible (e.g. hourly), check `expires_at` — expired → logout; within\nrefresh threshold → `refresh()` (single-flight: never two concurrent refreshes);\nthen `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user incl. profile image\npath. Guard all listener registration with `browser` (no SSR access to\n`document`). Follow the existing `UserNotifications` pattern\n(`visibilitychange` + interval, interval stopped while hidden). The routine\ncheck is a local date comparison — no network unless action is needed.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts\ndepends: TASK-1\nrisk: medium — new lifecycle listeners and async races; must not double-refresh,\nmust behave sanely on the desktop/mobile shells (app resume vs. tab visibility).\n\nTASK-3: Global 401 recovery in `ApiService` — logout strictly as the last\nresort. On a 401 from a non-auth endpoint, run a recovery ladder:\n(a) re-read the persisted auth from localStorage — if another tab refreshed\nthe token (multi-tab staleness), adopt it and retry the request (covers\n\"stale token although user is still authed\"); (b) otherwise single-flight\n`refresh()` and retry the original request exactly once with the new token;\n(c) only log out (with UI notification + redirect via TASK-5) if the refresh\nitself fails with a definitive auth rejection. Network errors (fetch\nrejection / offline) must NOT log out — they are transient and Layer 2\nre-checks on `online`. Must explicitly bypass the auth endpoints\n(`auth.login`, `auth.refresh`, forgot/reset password, passkey authenticate) —\na failed login legitimately returns 401 and must not trigger recovery. Never\nretry a request more than once. New user-visible strings must be added to all\nfour i18n files.\nfiles: src/lib/services/ApiService.ts, src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts,\nsrc/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2\nrisk: high — retry-on-401 logic can loop or misfire; several endpoints return\n401 for normal reasons; `postRaw` parses error bodies and needs care.\n\nTASK-4: Stop swallowing failed mutations for the reported symptom: surface\n`Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures via `UiNotifications.error()`\n(translation-aware), keeping the user's input in the modal instead of\ndiscarding it. Do not refactor other stores in this job.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts,\nsrc/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\ndepends: TASK-3 (so 401s are recovered rather than toasted twice)\nrisk: low — small, local change; i18n sync is enforced by `npm run check`.\n\nTASK-5: Make the root layout react to a mid-session logout: the auth guard in\n`+layout.svelte` only runs in `onMount`, so `loggedIn` flipping to false after\nTASK-2/TASK-3 leaves the user on a dead page. Add a reactive guard (e.g.\n`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn`) that redirects to login, without fighting the\nexisting onMount guard or triggering on auth/setup routes.\nfiles: src/routes/+layout.svelte\ndepends: TASK-2, TASK-3\nrisk: low-medium — navigation side effects; must not redirect-loop.\n\nTASK-6: Audit the previous profile-image fix for redundancy: with resume-driven\n`loadAdditionalData()` in place, check whether the earlier change (re-fetch of\n`/users/me` after login/`load()`, `profileCache`) still guards a distinct\nscenario (e.g. image re-upload changing the storage path, cache busting) and\nkeep or remove it with a written justification in implementation.md.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte,\nsrc/routes/profile/+page.svelte\ndepends: TASK-2\nrisk: low-medium — removing it without confirming the covered scenario could\nre-break the profile image.\n\nTASK-7: Verify: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`; manually simulate\nthe stale session (dev API with short token TTL or hand-edited `auth` localStorage\nentry: (a) expired token + resume from background → refreshed-and-recovered if\nthe backend honors a grace window, otherwise clean logout — determine which;\n(b) near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, notes create works; (c) invalid\ntoken server-side → 401 recovery ladder incl. localStorage adoption for the\nmulti-tab case; (d) offline/fetch-rejection → no logout, transient only).\nDeduced from the client (single bearer token, refresh authenticates with the\ncurrent token, empty body): the two open backend facts — (1) does refresh\naccept an already-expired token, (2) is the old token revoked on rotation —\nare to be probed empirically (curl dev API) and recorded here; the\nimplementation is deliberately agnostic to both (see recovery ladder), they\nonly pin down expected outcomes for (a) and (c). Document steps/results in\nimplementation.md.\nfiles: docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6\nrisk: low — verification only; no component-test infra exists, so manual steps\nare required.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":133,"totalLines":133,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791394510832,"end":1791394511301}},"id":"prt_1176ef7aa001Ks1Y4G2vLkH915","sessionID":"ses_ee8912192ffeUaFB6dscdlJxUU","messageID":"msg_1176ef0d3001maBicts6m7pQnX"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791394511416,"sessionID":"ses_ee8912192ffeUaFB6dscdlJxUU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_CUiYLGXbi75bh30RMI2k3784","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: reload after time away\n2: \n3: id: cover\n4: status: open\n5: developer: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Summary\n11: \n12: A permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\n13: stayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\n14: feature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\n15: closed and \"nothing happened\") and the in-memory user — including\n16: `profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\n17: `Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\n18: \n19: Implemented as a layered fix:\n20: \n21: - **TASK-1** — all state stores now share `Auth`'s single `ApiService` instance\n22:   instead of snapshotting the token at construction, so a runtime refresh\n23:   reaches every request. Logout clears the token on that shared instance.\n24: - **TASK-2** — `Auth` re-validates the session when the app resumes\n25:   (`visibilitychange` → visible, `online`) and on a low-frequency interval while\n26:   visible: expired/near-expiry → single-flight `refresh()`, then\n27:   `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user; definitive refresh\n28:   rejection → logout.\n29: - **TASK-3** — `ApiService` runs a global 401 recovery ladder for non-auth\n30:   endpoints: adopt another tab's fresher persisted token, else single-flight\n31:   refresh, retry the original request exactly once; only a definitive refresh\n32:   rejection logs out. Auth endpoints and network errors never trigger recovery.\n33: - **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures are surfaced via\n34:   `UiNotifications.error()` (translation-aware) instead of being swallowed, and\n35:   the modal + user input are kept so the entry can be retried.\n36: - **TASK-5** — the root layout reacts to a mid-session logout (`$effect` on\n37:   `auth.loggedIn`) and redirects to login/setup with a session-expired notice.\n38: - **TASK-6** — audit: keep the earlier profile-image fix; it covers a distinct\n39:   failure mode (transient/cross-origin image fetch) and is not made redundant\n40:   by the resume-driven `loadAdditionalData()`.\n41: - **TASK-7** — verification; see below.\n42: \n43: ## Changes\n44: \n45: TASK-1 — shared session ApiService\n46: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `clear()` now calls\n47:   `apiService.updateAuthToken(null)` so no store keeps sending a revoked token.\n48: - `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` (33 stores) — `this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`\n49:   replacing `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`; `Finances`/`Todos` change\n50:   their constructor default parameter to `auth.apiService`.\n51: - `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`, `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts` —\n52:   updated to assert stores share the instance (and the mock auth exposes it).\n53: \n54: TASK-2 — resume-driven session validation\n55: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` (hourly),\n56:   `startSessionMonitor()` registering `visibilitychange` + `online` (guarded by\n57:   `browser`), interval started while visible and stopped while hidden,\n58:   `validateSession()` doing the local `expires_at` comparison and only touching\n59:   the network when action is needed, then `loadAdditionalData()`. `refresh()` is\n60:   single-flight (`refreshInFlight`) and `performRefresh()` refreshes the shared\n61:   instance's token.\n62: \n63: TASK-3 — global 401 recovery\n64: - `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` — `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list,\n65:   `setUnauthorizedHandler()`, `fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request\n66:   method) which retries exactly once with the current token after a successful\n67:   recovery, and lets network errors propagate untouched. `updateAuthToken` now\n68:   accepts `null`.\n69: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `recoverFromUnauthorized()` /\n70:   `performRecovery()` (single-flight) ladder: (a) `adoptExternalSession()` reads\n71:   the persisted auth (multi-tab adoption), (b) `refresh()`, (c) logout only on a\n72:   definitive refresh rejection.\n73: - `tests/unit/services/ApiService.test.ts` — new \"401 recovery\" cases: retry\n74:   once with the fresh token, no retry when recovery declines, no recovery for\n75:   auth endpoints, no recovery on network error.\n76: - `tests/unit/auth/Auth.test.ts` — mock ApiService exposes\n77:   `setUnauthorizedHandler`.\n78: \n79: TASK-4 — surface failed note mutations\n80: - `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts` — `ts`/`notifications` context fields;\n81:   `create()` and `createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` on failure and\n82:   keep `inputValue`/`createParent`/`modalOpen`; the modal is closed by the store\n83:   on success instead of optimistically by the caller.\n84: - `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` — removed the optimistic `notes.closeModal()`\n85:   before create/confirm so a failed attempt leaves the modal (and the user's\n86:   input) open. (Needed to fulfil \"keep the input in the modal\"; the store now\n87:   owns success-close, which also handles the edit path whose return value is\n88:   `null`.)\n89: - `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts` + `src/lib/types/translation.ts` —\n90:   `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`.\n91: - `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` — stubs `getTranslation`/`getUiNotifications`,\n92:   asserts the error notification and that input/modal are retained on failure.\n93: \n94: TASK-5 — reactive mid-session logout\n95: - `src/routes/+layout.svelte` — imports `getUiNotifications`; `$effect` tracks\n96:   `auth.loggedIn`: on a logged-in → logged-out transition on a protected route it\n97:   shows `auth.session_expired` and redirects to login/setup. Auth/setup routes\n98:   and manual logout (`/auth/logout`) are excluded, so no redirect loop.\n99: \n100: TASK-6 — profile-image audit (no code change)\n101: - Keep `src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard and\n102:   `src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-on-error + letter\n103:   fallback. Rationale: the resume work fixes *stale data* (an expired token\n104:   hiding a newer `profile_image_path`), while the earlier fix addresses a\n105:   *broken in-session image fetch* — the SW previously answered the cross-origin\n106:   `<img>` with a synthetic `503`, and `<img>` never retries, so no amount of\n107:   resume-time `loadAdditionalData()` recovers it. `loadAdditionalData()` (boot /\n108:   login / resume) and `profileCache` (other users' public profiles for\n109:   `getPublicProfile`) remain independently necessary. Both fixes are\n110:   complementary; nothing was removed.\n111: \n112: ## Verification (TASK-7)\n113: \n114: Commands (this worktree, node 22):\n115: \n116: - `npm run check` — **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n117: - `npm test` — 53/54 files pass, **715 tests pass**. One unrelated pre-existing\n118:   failure: `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\n119:   requested color classes`, which expects `.bg-blue-50`/`.text-blue-600` while\n120:   the unchanged component uses theme classes (`bg-c-btn/10`, `text-c-btn`).\n121:   Neither the component nor the test is touched by this job.\n122: - `npm run lint` — ESLint on all changed files is **clean**. `prettier --check`\n123:   fails repo-wide (402 files) including files untouched by this job (and even\n124:   `HEAD` versions of unchanged files), i.e. pre-existing drift with the installed\n125:   prettier 3.6.2 + tailwind plugin; not introduced here.\n126: - Backend probes: **not possible in this environment** — no dev API is running\n127:   (`http://localhost:8000` refused). The two open backend facts (does `POST\n128:   /auth/refresh` accept an already-expired token? is the old token revoked on\n129:   rotation?) therefore remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately\n130:   agnostic (recovery ladder), so both answers are handled.\n131: \n132: Manual simulation steps to run against a dev API (or a hand-edited `auth`\n133: localStorage entry):\n134: \n135: - (a) Expired token + resume from background → `validateSession` attempts\n136:   `refresh()`; if the backend honors a grace window the request is recovered, if\n137:   not the user is cleanly logged out with the session-expired notice. Determine\n138:   which by observing the refresh response.\n139: - (b) Near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, then `loadAdditionalData()`; notes\n140:   create succeeds.\n141: - (c) Server-invalid token → 401 recovery ladder: with another tab holding a\n142:   fresher token, adopt + retry; otherwise refresh + retry once; only a rejected\n143:   refresh logs out.\n144: - (d) Offline/fetch rejection → no recovery, no logout (transient); re-checked on\n145:   the `online` event.\n146: \n147: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n148: \n149: - Eight components still build their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())`\n150:   (`dashboard/Inspiration`, `libraries/shared/Recommender`,\n151:   `calendars/ShareCalendarModal`, `settings/ExportSettings`,\n152:   `settings/TelegramBotConnection`, and the three\n153:   `settings/notifications/Manage*` components). They are outside TASK-1's\n154:   `state/*` scope, so they still snapshot the token and have no 401 handler and\n155:   can drift during a long-lived session. Worth converting to `auth.apiService` in\n156:   a follow-up.\n157: - `NavProfileEntry`'s `failed` flag resets only when `imagePath` changes, so a\n158:   transient image failure that later becomes loadable within the same session\n159:   (same path) still shows the letter fallback until navigation/reload.\n160: - Pre-existing repo-wide `prettier --check` drift and the unrelated\n161:   `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (both present before this job).\n\n(End of file - total 161 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nA permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\nstayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\nfeature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\nclosed and \"nothing happened\") and the in-memory user — including\n`profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\n`Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\n\nImplemented as a layered fix:\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nA permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\nstayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\nfeature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\nclosed and \"nothing happened\") and the in-memory user — including\n`profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\n`Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\n\nImplemented as a layered fix:\n\n- **TASK-1** — all state stores now share `Auth`'s single `ApiService` instance\n  instead of snapshotting the token at construction, so a runtime refresh\n  reaches every request. Logout clears the token on that shared instance.\n- **TASK-2** — `Auth` re-validates the session when the app resumes\n  (`visibilitychange` → visible, `online`) and on a low-frequency interval while\n  visible: expired/near-expiry → single-flight `refresh()`, then\n  `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user; definitive refresh\n  rejection → logout.\n- **TASK-3** — `ApiService` runs a global 401 recovery ladder for non-auth\n  endpoints: adopt another tab's fresher persisted token, else single-flight\n  refresh, retry the original request exactly once; only a definitive refresh\n  rejection logs out. Auth endpoints and network errors never trigger recovery.\n- **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures are surfaced via\n  `UiNotifications.error()` (translation-aware) instead of being swallowed, and\n  the modal + user input are kept so the entry can be retried.\n- **TASK-5** — the root layout reacts to a mid-session logout (`$effect` on\n  `auth.loggedIn`) and redirects to login/setup with a session-expired notice.\n- **TASK-6** — audit: keep the earlier profile-image fix; it covers a distinct\n  failure mode (transient/cross-origin image fetch) and is not made redundant\n  by the resume-driven `loadAdditionalData()`.\n- **TASK-7** — verification; see below.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1 — shared session ApiService\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `clear()` now calls\n  `apiService.updateAuthToken(null)` so no store keeps sending a revoked token.\n- `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` (33 stores) — `this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`\n  replacing `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`; `Finances`/`Todos` change\n  their constructor default parameter to `auth.apiService`.\n- `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`, `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts` —\n  updated to assert stores share the instance (and the mock auth exposes it).\n\nTASK-2 — resume-driven session validation\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` (hourly),\n  `startSessionMonitor()` registering `visibilitychange` + `online` (guarded by\n  `browser`), interval started while visible and stopped while hidden,\n  `validateSession()` doing the local `expires_at` comparison and only touching\n  the network when action is needed, then `loadAdditionalData()`. `refresh()` is\n  single-flight (`refreshInFlight`) and `performRefresh()` refreshes the shared\n  instance's token.\n\nTASK-3 — global 401 recovery\n- `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` — `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list,\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler()`, `fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request\n  method) which retries exactly once with the current token after a successful\n  recovery, and lets network errors propagate untouched. `updateAuthToken` now\n  accepts `null`.\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `recoverFromUnauthorized()` /\n  `performRecovery()` (single-flight) ladder: (a) `adoptExternalSession()` reads\n  the persisted auth (multi-tab adoption), (b) `refresh()`, (c) logout only on a\n  definitive refresh rejection.\n- `tests/unit/services/ApiService.test.ts` — new \"401 recovery\" cases: retry\n  once with the fresh token, no retry when recovery declines, no recovery for\n  auth endpoints, no recovery on network error.\n- `tests/unit/auth/Auth.test.ts` — mock ApiService exposes\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler`.\n\nTASK-4 — surface failed note mutations\n- `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts` — `ts`/`notifications` context fields;\n  `create()` and `createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` on failure and\n  keep `inputValue`/`createParent`/`modalOpen`; the modal is closed by the store\n  on success instead of optimistically by the caller.\n- `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` — removed the optimistic `notes.closeModal()`\n  before create/confirm so a failed attempt leaves the modal (and the user's\n  input) open. (Needed to fulfil \"keep the input in the modal\"; the store now\n  owns success-close, which also handles the edit path whose return value is\n  `null`.)\n- `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts` + `src/lib/types/translation.ts` —\n  `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`.\n- `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` — stubs `getTranslation`/`getUiNotifications`,\n  asserts the error notification and that input/modal are retained on failure.\n\nTASK-5 — reactive mid-session logout\n- `src/routes/+layout.svelte` — imports `getUiNotifications`; `$effect` tracks\n  `auth.loggedIn`: on a logged-in → logged-out transition on a protected route it\n  shows `auth.session_expired` and redirects to login/setup. Auth/setup routes\n  and manual logout (`/auth/logout`) are excluded, so no redirect loop.\n\nTASK-6 — profile-image audit (no code change)\n- Keep `src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard and\n  `src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-on-error + letter\n  fallback. Rationale: the resume work fixes *stale data* (an expired token\n  hiding a newer `profile_image_path`), while the earlier fix addresses a\n  *broken in-session image fetch* — the SW previously answered the cross-origin\n  `<img>` with a synthetic `503`, and `<img>` never retries, so no amount of\n  resume-time `loadAdditionalData()` recovers it. `loadAdditionalData()` (boot /\n  login / resume) and `profileCache` (other users' public profiles for\n  `getPublicProfile`) remain independently necessary. Both fixes are\n  complementary; nothing was removed.\n\n## Verification (TASK-7)\n\nCommands (this worktree, node 22):\n\n- `npm run check` — **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n- `npm test` — 53/54 files pass, **715 tests pass**. One unrelated pre-existing\n  failure: `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\n  requested color classes`, which expects `.bg-blue-50`/`.text-blue-600` while\n  the unchanged component uses theme classes (`bg-c-btn/10`, `text-c-btn`).\n  Neither the component nor the test is touched by this job.\n- `npm run lint` — ESLint on all changed files is **clean**. `prettier --check`\n  fails repo-wide (402 files) including files untouched by this job (and even\n  `HEAD` versions of unchanged files), i.e. pre-existing drift with the installed\n  prettier 3.6.2 + tailwind plugin; not introduced here.\n- Backend probes: **not possible in this environment** — no dev API is running\n  (`http://localhost:8000` refused). The two open backend facts (does `POST\n  /auth/refresh` accept an already-expired token? is the old token revoked on\n  rotation?) therefore remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately\n  agnostic (recovery ladder), so both answers are handled.\n\nManual simulation steps to run against a dev API (or a hand-edited `auth`\nlocalStorage entry):\n\n- (a) Expired token + resume from background → `validateSession` attempts\n  `refresh()`; if the backend honors a grace window the request is recovered, if\n  not the user is cleanly logged out with the session-expired notice. Determine\n  which by observing the refresh response.\n- (b) Near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, then `loadAdditionalData()`; notes\n  create succeeds.\n- (c) Server-invalid token → 401 recovery ladder: with another tab holding a\n  fresher token, adopt + retry; otherwise refresh + retry once; only a rejected\n  refresh logs out.\n- (d) Offline/fetch rejection → no recovery, no logout (transient); re-checked on\n  the `online` event.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Eight components still build their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())`\n  (`dashboard/Inspiration`, `libraries/shared/Recommender`,\n  `calendars/ShareCalendarModal`, `settings/ExportSettings`,\n  `settings/TelegramBotConnection`, and the three\n  `settings/notifications/Manage*` components). They are outside TASK-1's\n  `state/*` scope, so they still snapshot the token and have no 401 handler and\n  can drift during a long-lived session. Worth converting to `auth.apiService` in\n  a follow-up.\n- `NavProfileEntry`'s `failed` flag resets only when `imagePath` changes, so a\n  transient image failure that later becomes loadable within the same session\n  (same path) still shows the letter fallback until navigation/reload.\n- Pre-existing repo-wide `prettier --check` drift and the unrelated\n  `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (both present before this job).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":161,"totalLines":161,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791394511013,"end":1791394511394}},"id":"prt_1176ef7fe001lNaM19gNYTHTTs","sessionID":"ses_ee8912192ffeUaFB6dscdlJxUU","messageID":"msg_1176ef0d3001maBicts6m7pQnX"}}
