{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395151815,"sessionID":"ses_ee8892f12ffe84r1wb0aepjgG5","part":{"id":"prt_11778b6e5001on1dV0yKixpCdZ","messageID":"msg_11778afd80011bcKwWaiH90rMK","sessionID":"ses_ee8892f12ffe84r1wb0aepjgG5","type":"text","text":"The worktree is clean. Here's what I found and did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe job `cover_reload-after-time-away` was **already fully implemented and committed** in a prior developer session (commit `7725ae4`) with its summary committed in `8a28a87`. I verified the implementation rather than re-doing it, since re-implementing complete, passing work would be redundant and risky.\n\n**Branch check:** `feature/cover_reload-after-time-away` matches the `branch:` field in `brief.md` — correct branch, no checkout needed.\n\n**Verification I ran:**\n- `npm run check` → **0 errors, 0 warnings**\n- `npm test` → **715 passed / 716**, the single failure being the unrelated, pre-existing `StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes` case documented in `implementation.md` (its component and test are untouched by this job)\n- Confirmed TASK-1 is applied across the state stores (27 use `this.auth.apiService`, `Finances`/`Todos` use `auth.apiService` as default param; the only remaining `new ApiService` in `state/` is `Auth`'s own instance, as intended)\n- Confirmed TASK-2 lifecycle monitor in `Auth.svelte.ts`, TASK-3 401 recovery ladder in `ApiService.ts`, TASK-4 error surfacing in `Notes.svelte.ts`, TASK-5 reactive guard in `+layout.svelte`\n- Confirmed the new i18n keys (`notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`) exist in all four languages and in `types/translation.ts`\n\n**Changes in this session:** none to source — only the harness session artifacts (`session.log`, `tokens.json`) were committed to leave the worktree clean. The `implementation.md` summary (including TASK-6 audit rationale and TASK-7 verification) is present and accurate.\n\n**Known issues** (from `implementation.md`, still open follow-ups, out of scope here):\n- Eight components still construct their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())` (dashboard/libraries/calendar/settings) so they can still drift on a long-lived session.\n- `NavProfileEntry`'s `failed` flag only resets when the image path changes.\n- Pre-existing repo-wide `prettier --check` drift and the unrelated `StatisticWidget` test failure (both predate this job).\n\nNo blocker requiring human input was encountered, so no `NEEDS-HUMAN-INPUT` line was needed.","time":{"start":1791395149541,"end":1791395151804}}}
