{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791395392922,"sessionID":"ses_ee88730eeffeRJKdaZ6r4Ci5uf","part":{"id":"prt_1177c6d8d001284jDb0fbqMuia","messageID":"msg_1177c65a4001DFUSMGD6YakTZW","sessionID":"ses_ee88730eeffeRJKdaZ6r4Ci5uf","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1791395396997,"sessionID":"ses_ee88730eeffeRJKdaZ6r4Ci5uf","part":{"id":"prt_1177c73e5001RZGr6KKGB2FMEq","messageID":"msg_1177c65a4001DFUSMGD6YakTZW","sessionID":"ses_ee88730eeffeRJKdaZ6r4Ci5uf","type":"text","text":"The job is complete. Here is what I found and did.\n\n## Situation\n\nThe workspace was **already fully implemented** by prior developer attempts on the correct branch (`feature/cover_reload-after-time-away`, matching `brief.md`). The implementation lives in commit `7725ae4` with the summary in `8a28a87`. Rather than duplicate/redo work (which risks breaking a correct change), I audited it against `tasks.md` and re-verified it.\n\n## What I verified (TASK-7)\n\n- **TASK-1** — all 33 stores use `this.auth.apiService` (grep confirms `new ApiService` only remains in `Auth` itself); `Auth.clear()` nulls the shared token.\n- **TASK-2** — `Auth` registers `visibilitychange` + `online` guarded by `browser`, an hourly interval started while visible/stopped while hidden, single-flight `refresh()`, then `loadAdditionalData()`.\n- **TASK-3** — `ApiService.fetchWithRecovery()` with an auth-endpoint bypass list, single retry, no recovery on network errors; `Auth` recovery ladder = adopt other-tab token → refresh → logout only on definitive rejection.\n- **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()`/`createCategory()` report via `UiNotifications.error()` and keep the modal/input on failure; the modal no longer closes optimistically.\n- **TASK-5** — reactive `$effect` in `+layout.svelte` redirects on a logged-in → logged-out transition, excluding auth/setup routes.\n- **TASK-6** — confirmed both earlier profile-image fixes are present on the branch (`src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard at line 54; `NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-then-letter fallback) and serve a **distinct** failure mode (transient cross-origin image fetch) from this job's stale-session fix — so keeping them is correct, not redundant.\n- i18n: `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired` present in en/de/es/fr and `types/translation.ts`.\n\n## Commands re-run\n\n- `npm run check` → **0 errors, 0 warnings**\n- `npm test` → **715 passed**, 1 failure that is pre-existing and unrelated (`tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget`, a file graph this job never touches)\n- `npx eslint` on all changed source files → clean\n\n## Commits added\n\n- `fc2fd99` `[cover] implementation: re-verify gates and finalize summary` — records the re-verification and the TASK-6 audit confirmation in `implementation.md`.\n- `e99512a` `[cover] chore: finalize session artifacts` — leaves the worktree clean.\n\nNo code changes were needed; the implementation already satisfies every task. Out-of-scope follow-up already documented: 8 non-store components still build their own `ApiService` and should be migrated in a separate job. No blockers.","time":{"start":1791395394533,"end":1791395396989}}}
