itionalData()`.\\n41: - **TASK-7** — verification; see below.\\n42: \\n43: ## Changes\\n44: \\n45: TASK-1 — shared session ApiService\\n46: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `clear()` now calls\\n47:   `apiService.updateAuthToken(null)` so no store keeps sending a revoked token.\\n48: - `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` (33 stores) — `this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`\\n49:   replacing `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`; `Finances`/`Todos` change\\n50:   their constructor default parameter to `auth.apiService`.\\n51: - `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`, `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts` —\\n52:   updated to assert stores share the instance (and the mock auth exposes it).\\n53: \\n54: TASK-2 — resume-driven session validation\\n55: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` (hourly),\\n56:   `startSessionMonitor()` registering `visibilitychange` + `online` (guarded by\\n57:   `browser`), interval started while visible and stopped while hidden,\\n58:   `validateSession()` doing the local `expires_at` comparison and only touching\\n59:   the network when action is needed, then `loadAdditionalData()`. `refresh()` is\\n60:   single-flight (`refreshInFlight`) and `performRefresh()` refreshes the shared\\n61:   instance's token.\\n62: \\n63: TASK-3 — global 401 recovery\\n64: - `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` — `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list,\\n65:   `setUnauthorizedHandler()`, `fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request\\n66:   method) which retries exactly once with the current token after a successful\\n67:   recovery, and lets network errors propagate untouched. `updateAuthToken` now\\n68:   accepts `null`.\\n69: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `recoverFromUnauthorized()` /\\n70:   `performRecovery()` (single-flight) ladder: (a) `adoptExternalSession()` reads\\n71:   the persisted auth (multi-tab adoption), (b) `refresh()`, (c) logout only on a\\n72:   definitive refresh rejection.\\n73: - `tests/unit/services/ApiService.test.ts` — new \\\"401 recovery\\\" cases: retry\\n74:   once with the fresh token, no retry when recovery declines, no recovery for\\n75:   auth endpoints, no recovery on network error.\\n76: - `tests/unit/auth/Auth.test.ts` — mock ApiService exposes\\n77:   `setUnauthorizedHandler`.\\n78: \\n79: TASK-4 — surface failed note mutations\\n80: - `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts` — `ts`/`notifications` context fields;\\n81:   `create()` and `createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` on failure and\\n82:   keep `inputValue`/`createParent`/`modalOpen`; the modal is closed by the store\\n83:   on success instead of optimistically by the caller.\\n84: - `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` — removed the optimistic `notes.closeModal()`\\n85:   before create/confirm so a failed attempt leaves the modal (and the user's\\n86:   input) open. (Needed to fulfil \\\"keep the input in the modal\\\"; the store now\\n87:   owns success-close, which also handles the edit path whose return value is\\n88:   `null`.)\\n89: - `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts` + `src/lib/types/translation.ts` —\\n90:   `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`.\\n91: - `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` — stubs `getTranslation`/`getUiNotifications`,\\n92:   asserts the error notification and that input/modal are retained on failure.\\n93: \\n94: TASK-5 — reactive mid-session logout\\n95: - `src/routes/+layout.svelte` — imports `getUiNotifications`; `$effect` tracks\\n96:   `auth.loggedIn`: on a logged-in → logged-out transition on a protected route it\\n97:   shows `auth.session_expired` and redirects to login/setup. Auth/setup routes\\n98:   and manual logout (`/auth/logout`) are excluded, so no redirect loop.\\n99: \\n100: TASK-6 — profile-image audit (no code change)\\n101: - Keep `src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard and\\n102:   `src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-on-error + letter\\n103:   fallback. Rationale: the resume work fixes *stale data* (an expired token\\n104:   hiding a newer `profile_image_path`), while the earlier fix addresses a\\n105:   *broken in-session image fetch* — the SW previously answered the cross-origin\\n106:   `<img>` with a synthetic `503`, and `<img>` never retries, so no amount of\\n107:   resume-time `loadAdditionalData()` recovers it. `loadAdditionalData()` (boot /\\n108:   login / resume) and `profileCache` (other users' public profiles for\\n109:   `getPublicProfile`) remain independently necessary. Both fixes are\\n110:   complementary; nothing was removed.\\n111: \\n112: ## Verification (TASK-7)\\n113: \\n114: Commands (this worktree, node 22):\\n115: \\n116: - `npm run check` — **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\\n117: - `npm test` — 53/54 files pass, **715 tests pass**. One unrelated pre-existing\\n118:   failure: `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\\n119:   requested color classes`, which expects `.bg-blue-50`/`.text-blue-600` while\\n120:   the unchanged component uses theme classes (`bg-c-btn/10`, `text-c-btn`).\\n121:   Neither the component nor the test is touched by this job.\\n122: - `npm run lint` — ESLint on all changed files is **clean**. `prettier --check`\\n123:   fails repo-wide (402 files) including files untouched by this job (and even\\n124:   `HEAD` versions of unchanged files), i.e. pre-existing drift with the installed\\n125:   prettier 3.6.2 + tailwind plugin; not introduced here.\\n126: - Backend probes: **not possible in this environment** — no dev API is running\\n127:   (`http://localhost:8000` refused). The two open backend facts (does `POST\\n128:   /auth/refresh` accept an already-expired token? is the old token revoked on\\n129:   rotation?) therefore remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately\\n130:   agnostic (recovery ladder), so both answers are handled.\\n131: - Re-verified in a follow-up pass (same worktree, node 22) — results unchanged\\n132:   and no code edits were needed: `npm run check` 0 errors / 0 warnings;\\n133:   `npm test` 715 passed with the same single unrelated pre-existing failure\\n134:   (`tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget`, a file graph this\\n135:   job does not touch); `npx eslint` clean on every changed source file. Also\\n136:   confirmed on the branch that TASK-6's audit is accurate: the service worker's\\n137:   same-origin GET guard (`src/service-worker.ts`) and `NavProfileEntry`'s\\n138:   retry-then-letter fallback are both present and independent of the resume\\n139:   work.\\n140: \\n141: Manual simulation steps to run against a dev API (or a hand-edited `auth`\\n142: localStorage entry):\\n143: \\n144: - (a) Expired token + resume from background → `validateSession` attempts\\n145:   `refresh()`; if the backend honors a grace window the request is recovered, if\\n146:   not the user is cleanly logged out with the session-expired notice. Determine\\n147:   which by observing the refresh response.\\n148: - (b) Near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, then `loadAdditionalData()`; notes\\n149:   create succeeds.\\n150: - (c) Server-invalid token → 401 recovery ladder: with another tab holding a\\n151:   fresher token, adopt + retry; otherwise refresh + retry once; only a rejected\\n152:   refresh logs out.\\n153: - (d) Offline/fetch rejection → no recovery, no logout (transient); re-checked on\\n154:   the `online` event.\\n155: \\n156: ## Known issues / follow-ups\\n157: \\n158: - Eight components still build their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())`\\n159:   (`dashboard/Inspiration`, `libraries/shared/Recommender`,\\n160:   `calendars/ShareCalendarModal`, `settings/ExportSettings`,\\n161:   `settings/TelegramBotConnection`, and the three\\n162:   `settings/notifications/Manage*` components). They are outside TASK-1's\\n163:   `state/*` scope, so they still snapshot the token and have no 401 handler and\\n164:   can drift during a long-lived session. Worth converting to `auth.apiService` in\\n165:   a follow-up.\\n166: - `NavProfileEntry`'s `failed` flag resets only when `imagePath` changes, so a\\n167:   transient image failure that later becomes loadable within the same session\\n168:   (same path) still shows the letter fallback until navigation/reload.\\n169: - Pre-existing repo-wide `prettier --check` drift and the unrelated\\n170:   `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (both present before this job).\\n\\n(End of file - total 170 lines)\\n</content>\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\\n# solyto frontend\\n\\n<!--\\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \\\"the agent\\\", not for one vendor.\\n-->\\n\\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\\n\\n## Stack\\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\\n\\n## Commands\\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\\n\\n## Hard rules\\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\\n\\n</system-reminder>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# Implementation: reload after time away\\n\\nid: cover\\nstatus: open\\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\\ndate: 2026-10-07\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nA permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\\nstayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\\nfeature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\\nclosed and \\\"nothing happened\\\") and the in-memory user — including\\n`profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\\n`Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\\n\\nImplemented as a layered fix:\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[\"/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\"],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md\",\"text\":\"# Implementation: reload after time away\\n\\nid: cover\\nstatus: open\\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\\ndate: 2026-10-07\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nA permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\\nstayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\\nfeature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\\nclosed and \\\"nothing happened\\\") and the in-memory user — including\\n`profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\\n`Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\\n\\nImplemented as a layered fix:\\n\\n- **TASK-1** — all state stores now share `Auth`'s single `ApiService` instance\\n  instead of snapshotting the token at construction, so a runtime refresh\\n  reaches every request. Logout clears the token on that shared instance.\\n- **TASK-2** — `Auth` re-validates the session when the app resumes\\n  (`visibilitychange` → visible, `online`) and on a low-frequency interval while\\n  visible: expired/near-expiry → single-flight `refresh()`, then\\n  `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user; definitive refresh\\n  rejection → logout.\\n- **TASK-3** — `ApiService` runs a global 401 recovery ladder for non-auth\\n  endpoints: adopt another tab's fresher persisted token, else single-flight\\n  refresh, retry the original request exactly once; only a definitive refresh\\n  rejection logs out. Auth endpoints and network errors never trigger recovery.\\n- **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures are surfaced via\\n  `UiNotifications.error()` (translation-aware) instead of being swallowed, and\\n  the modal + user input are kept so the entry can be retried.\\n- **TASK-5** — the root layout reacts to a mid-session logout (`$effect` on\\n  `auth.loggedIn`) and redirects to login/setup with a session-expired notice.\\n- **TASK-6** — audit: keep the earlier profile-image fix; it covers a distinct\\n  failure mode (transient/cross-origin image fetch) and is not made redundant\\n  by the resume-driven `loadAdditionalData()`.\\n- **TASK-7** — verification; see below.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1 — shared session ApiService\\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `clear()` now calls\\n  `apiService.updateAuthToken(null)` so no store keeps sending a revoked token.\\n- `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` (33 stores) — `this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`\\n  replacing `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`; `Finances`/`Todos` change\\n  their constructor default parameter to `auth.apiService`.\\n- `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`, `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts` —\\n  updated to assert stores share the instance (and the mock auth exposes it).\\n\\nTASK-2 — resume-driven session validation\\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` (hourly),\\n  `startSessionMonitor()` registering `visibilitychange` + `online` (guarded by\\n  `browser`), interval started while visible and stopped while hidden,\\n  `validateSession()` doing the local `expires_at` comparison and only touching\\n  the network when action is needed, then `loadAdditionalData()`. `refresh()` is\\n  single-flight (`refreshInFlight`) and `performRefresh()` refreshes the shared\\n  instance's token.\\n\\nTASK-3 — global 401 recovery\\n- `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` — `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list,\\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler()`, `fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request\\n  method) which retries exactly once with the current token after a successful\\n  recovery, and lets network errors propagate untouched. `updateAuthToken` now\\n  accepts `null`.\\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `recoverFromUnauthorized()` /\\n  `performRecovery()` (single-flight) ladder: (a) `adoptExternalSession()` reads\\n  the persisted auth (multi-tab adoption), (b) `refresh()`, (c) logout only on a\\n  definitive refresh rejection.\\n- `tests/unit/services/ApiService.test.ts` — new \\\"401 recovery\\\" cases: retry\\n  once with the fresh token, no retry when recovery declines, no recovery for\\n  auth endpoints, no recovery on network error.\\n- `tests/unit/auth/Auth.test.ts` — mock ApiService exposes\\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler`.\\n\\nTASK-4 — surface failed note mutations\\n- `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts` — `ts`/`notifications` context fields;\\n  `create()` and `createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` on failure and\\n  keep `inputValue`/`createParent`/`modalOpen`; the modal is closed by the store\\n  on success instead of optimistically by the caller.\\n- `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` — removed the optimistic `notes.closeModal()`\\n  before create/confirm so a failed attempt leaves the modal (and the user's\\n  input) open. (Needed to fulfil \\\"keep the input in the modal\\\"; the store now\\n  owns success-close, which also handles the edit path whose return value is\\n  `null`.)\\n- `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts` + `src/lib/types/translation.ts` —\\n  `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`.\\n- `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` — stubs `getTranslation`/`getUiNotifications`,\\n  asserts the error notification and that input/modal are retained on failure.\\n\\nTASK-5 — reactive mid-session logout\\n- `src/routes/+layout.svelte` — imports `getUiNotifications`; `$effect` tracks\\n  `auth.loggedIn`: on a logged-in → logged-out transition on a protected route it\\n  shows `auth.session_expired` and redirects to login/setup. Auth/setup routes\\n  and manual logout (`/auth/logout`) are excluded, so no redirect loop.\\n\\nTASK-6 — profile-image audit (no code change)\\n- Keep `src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard and\\n  `src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-on-error + letter\\n  fallback. Rationale: the resume work fixes *stale data* (an expired token\\n  hiding a newer `profile_image_path`), while the earlier fix addresses a\\n  *broken in-session image fetch* — the SW previously answered the cross-origin\\n  `<img>` with a synthetic `503`, and `<img>` never retries, so no amount of\\n  resume-time `loadAdditionalData()` recovers it. `loadAdditionalData()` (boot /\\n  login / resume) and `profileCache` (other users' public profiles for\\n  `getPublicProfile`) remain independently necessary. Both fixes are\\n  complementary; nothing was removed.\\n\\n## Verification (TASK-7)\\n\\nCommands (this worktree, node 22):\\n\\n- `npm run check` — **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\\n- `npm test` — 53/54 files pass, **715 tests pass**. One unrelated pre-existing\\n  failure: `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\\n  requested color classes`, which expects `.bg-blue-50`/`.text-blue-600` while\\n  the unchanged component uses theme classes (`bg-c-btn/10`, `text-c-btn`).\\n  Neither the component nor the test is touched by this job.\\n- `npm run lint` — ESLint on all changed files is **clean**. `prettier --check`\\n  fails repo-wide (402 files) including files untouched by this job (and even\\n  `HEAD` versions of unchanged files), i.e. pre-existing drift with the installed\\n  prettier 3.6.2 + tailwind plugin; not introduced here.\\n- Backend probes: **not possible in this environment** — no dev API is running\\n  (`http://localhost:8000` refused). The two open backend facts (does `POST\\n  /auth/refresh` accept an already-expired token? is the old token revoked on\\n  rotation?) therefore remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately\\n  agnostic (recovery ladder), so both answers are handled.\\n- Re-verified in a follow-up pass (same worktree, node 22) — results unchanged\\n  and no code edits were needed: `npm run check` 0 errors / 0 warnings;\\n  `npm test` 715 passed with the same single unrelated pre-existing failure\\n  (`tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget`, a file graph this\\n  job does not touch); `npx eslint` clean on every changed source file. Also\\n  confirmed on the branch that TASK-6's audit is accurate: the service worker's\\n  same-origin GET guard (`src/service-worker.ts`) and `NavProfileEntry`'s\\n  retry-then-letter fallback are both present and independent of the resume\\n  work.\\n\\nManual simulation steps to run against a dev API (or a hand-edited `auth`\\nlocalStorage entry):\\n\\n- (a) Expired token + resume from background → `validateSession` attempts\\n  `refresh()`; if the backend honors a grace window the request is recovered, if\\n  not the user is cleanly logged out with the session-expired notice. Determine\\n  which by observing the refresh response.\\n- (b) Near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, then `loadAdditionalData()`; notes\\n  create succeeds.\\n- (c) Server-invalid token → 401 recovery ladder: with another tab holding a\\n  fresher token, adopt + retry; otherwise refresh + retry once; only a rejected\\n  refresh logs out.\\n- (d) Offline/fetch rejection → no recovery, no logout (transient); re-checked on\\n  the `online` event.\\n\\n## Known issues / follow-ups\\n\\n- Eight components still build their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())`\\n  (`dashboard/Inspiration`, `libraries/shared/Recommender`,\\n  `calendars/ShareCalendarModal`, `settings/ExportSettings`,\\n  `settings/TelegramBotConnection`, and the three\\n  `settings/notifications/Manage*` components). They are outside TASK-1's\\n  `state/*` scope, so they still snapshot the token and have no 401 handler and\\n  can drift during a long-lived session. Worth converting to `auth.apiService` in\\n  a follow-up.\\n- `NavProfileEntry`'s `failed` flag resets only when `imagePath` changes, so a\\n  transient image failure that later becomes loadable within the same session\\n  (same path) still shows the letter fallback until navigation/reload.\\n- Pre-existing repo-wide `prettier --check` drift and the unrelated\\n  `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (both present before this job).\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":170,\"totalLines\":170,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791395537463,\"end\":1791395537471}},\"id\":\"prt_1177ea1e7001lZnM00x1zaePA9\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177e990f001sQ4jouZfETQy9V\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791395537503,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1177ea0f6001y5bkwmdDKtzjTQ\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177e990f001sQ4jouZfETQy9V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"This job appears to have prior session history. Let me understand the current state.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791395537142,\"end\":1791395537494}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791395537609,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1177ea2b1001RYFbbLO2WpaT3Y\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177e990f001sQ4jouZfETQy9V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":18152,\"input\":412,\"output\":123,\"reasoning\":81,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":17536}},\"cost\":0.000236808}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791395538793,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1177ea767001DcKYm01UXyqzje\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177ea2bb001eU60FlxH9hC93v\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791395541389,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1177eafba0010I5x3jyk2ovBy6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1177ea2bb001eU60FlxH9hC93v\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The implementation appears already complete from a prior session. Let me inspect the uncommitted artifacts and verify the current state.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791395540922,\"end\":1791395541386}}}\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tokens.json b/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tokens.json\nindex ebbf958..225c213 100644\n--- a/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tokens.json\n+++ b/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tokens.json\n@@ -78,5 +78,15 @@\n     \"cacheReadTokens\": 2118144,\n     \"reasoningTokens\": 17309,\n     \"costUSD\": 0.030757181999999997\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"agent\": \"developer\",\n+    \"attempt\": 9,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-07T17:52:02.332036502Z\",\n+    \"inputTokens\": 52988,\n+    \"outputTokens\": 2600,\n+    \"cacheReadTokens\": 541312,\n+    \"reasoningTokens\": 4766,\n+    \"costUSD\": 0.013991736\n   }\n ]\n\\ No newline at end of file\n=== ls job dir ===\ntotal 3808\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 1002 1002    4096 Oct  7 17:32 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 4 1002 1002    4096 Aug 19 15:45 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1002 1002    1353 Aug 19 15:47 brief.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1002 1002    9654 Oct  7 17:49 implementation.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1002 1002 3852086 Oct  7 17:52 session.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1002 1002    7481 Aug 19 16:15 tasks.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1002 1002    2241 Oct  7 17:52 tokens.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1002 1002     446 Aug 19 15:45 verdict.md\n=== gitignored? ===\nnot ignored\n","exit":0,"truncated":true,"outputPath":"/home/claude/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1177eb1cd001zK7ZlXlmv9ifdY"},"title":"cd /workspace && git diff -- docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/session.log docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tokens.json; echo \"=== ls job dir ===\"; ls -la docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/; echo \"=== gitignored? ===\"; git check-ignore docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tokens.json docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/session.log || echo \"not ignored\"","time":{"start":1791395541379,"end":1791395541464}},"id":"prt_1177eb03a001s60zx7VTFArinC","sessionID":"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm","messageID":"msg_1177ea2bb001eU60FlxH9hC93v"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1791395541539,"sessionID":"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm","part":{"id":"prt_1177eb202001gGFrrk52QBxOhM","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"","messageID":"msg_1177ea2bb001eU60FlxH9hC93v","sessionID":"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":24232,"input":5562,"output":169,"reasoning":453,"cache":{"write":0,"read":18048}},"cost":0.001261644}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1791395543097,"sessionID":"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm","part":{"id":"prt_1177eb836001DZ5opY7kF7iKch","messageID":"msg_1177eb20d001Ks658inCLXX4c6","sessionID":"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm","snapshot":"","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791395545978,"sessionID":"ses_ee8818e60ffetGBXJ1ST4fwJTm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_aVOwqyxP6w3RjqlogIHz1936","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/src/lib/services/ApiService.ts"},"output":"<path>/workspace/src/lib/services/ApiService.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import type { CreateResponse, GetResponse, ListResponse, PostResponse } from '$lib/types/api';\n2: import { apiRoutes } from '$lib/config/apiRoutes';\n3: \n4: // Endpoints where a 401 is a legitimate, expected auth failure (bad credentials,\n5: // expired refresh token, failed passkey authentication) rather than a stale\n6: // session. Recovery must never run for these, otherwise a failed login would\n7: // trigger a refresh/logout loop.\n8: const AUTH_ENDPOINTS: string[] = [\n9: \tapiRoutes.auth.login,\n10: \tapiRoutes.auth.refresh,\n11: \tapiRoutes.auth.register,\n12: \tapiRoutes.auth.verify,\n13: \tapiRoutes.auth.forgotPassword,\n14: \tapiRoutes.auth.resetPassword,\n15: \tapiRoutes.auth.passkeys.authenticateOptions,\n16: \tapiRoutes.auth.passkeys.authenticate\n17: ];\n18: \n19: export default class ApiService {\n20: \tauthToken: string | null = null;\n21: \tprivate unauthorizedHandler: (() => Promise<boolean>) | null = null;\n22: \n23: \tconstructor(authToken: string | null = null) {\n24: \t\tthis.authToken = authToken;\n25: \t}\n26: \n27: \tupdateAuthToken(authToken: string | null): void {\n28: \t\tthis.authToken = authToken;\n29: \t}\n30: \n31: \t// The owner of the session (Auth) registers a single recovery routine here.\n32: \t// It is expected to adopt a token refreshed by another tab, or refresh this\n33: \t// session, and return true when a retry with a fresh token makes sense.\n34: \tsetUnauthorizedHandler(handler: () => Promise<boolean>): void {\n35: \t\tthis.unauthorizedHandler = handler;\n36: \t}\n37: \n38: \tprivate isAuthEndpoint(endpoint: string): boolean {\n39: \t\treturn AUTH_ENDPOINTS.some((authEndpoint) => endpoint.startsWith(authEndpoint));\n40: \t}\n41: \n42: \t// Runs a request; on a 401 from a non-auth endpoint asks the session owner\n43: \t// to recover and, if it did, retries the same request exactly once with the\n44: \t// current token. Network errors (a rejected fetch) propagate untouched — they\n45: \t// are transient and must never trigger recovery/logout.\n46: \tprivate async fetchWithRecovery(endpoint: string, init: RequestInit): Promise<Response> {\n47: \t\tconst res = await fetch(endpoint, init);\n48: \n49: \t\tif (res.status !== 401 || !this.unauthorizedHandler || this.isAuthEndpoint(endpoint)) {\n50: \t\t\treturn res;\n51: \t\t}\n52: \n53: \t\tconst recovered = await this.unauthorizedHandler();\n54: \t\tif (!recovered) return res;\n55: \n56: \t\tconst headers = { ...(init.headers as Record<string, string>) };\n57: \t\tif (this.authToken) {\n58: \t\t\theaders['Authorization'] = 'Bearer ' + this.authToken;\n59: \t\t} else {\n60: \t\t\tdelete headers['Authorization'];\n61: \t\t}\n62: \n63: \t\treturn fetch(endpoint, { ...init, headers });\n64: \t}\n65: \n66: \tasync list(endpoint: string): Promise<ListResponse | null> {\n67: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, { headers: this.getApiHeader() });\n68: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n69: \t}\n70: \n71: \tasync get(endpoint: string, id: string | number | null): Promise<GetResponse | null> {\n72: \t\tif (typeof id === 'string') {\n73: \t\t\tendpoint = endpoint.replace('%s', id);\n74: \t\t} else if (typeof id === 'number') {\n75: \t\t\tendpoint = endpoint.replace('%d', id.toString());\n76: \t\t}\n77: \n78: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, { headers: this.getApiHeader() });\n79: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n80: \t}\n81: \n82: \tasync create(endpoint: string, body: object): Promise<CreateResponse | null> {\n83: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n84: \t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n85: \t\t\theaders: this.getApiHeaderWithBody(),\n86: \t\t\tbody: JSON.stringify(body)\n87: \t\t});\n88: \n89: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n90: \t}\n91: \n92: \tasync createWithStatus(endpoint: string, body: object): Promise<{ ok: boolean; status: number }> {\n93: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n94: \t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n95: \t\t\theaders: this.getApiHeaderWithBody(),\n96: \t\t\tbody: JSON.stringify(body)\n97: \t\t});\n98: \n99: \t\treturn { ok: res.ok, status: res.status };\n100: \t}\n101: \n102: \tasync delete(endpoint: string, id: string | number): Promise<boolean> {\n103: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(\n104: \t\t\ttypeof id === 'string'\n105: \t\t\t\t? endpoint.replace('%s', id)\n106: \t\t\t\t: endpoint.replace('%d', id.toString()),\n107: \t\t\t{ method: 'DELETE', headers: this.getApiHeader() }\n108: \t\t);\n109: \n110: \t\treturn Promise.resolve(res.ok);\n111: \t}\n112: \n113: \tasync update(endpoint: string, id: string | number, body: object): Promise<boolean> {\n114: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(\n115: \t\t\ttypeof id === 'string'\n116: \t\t\t\t? endpoint.replace('%s', id)\n117: \t\t\t\t: endpoint.replace('%d', id.toString()),\n118: \t\t\t{ method: 'PUT', headers: this.getApiHeaderWithBody(), body: JSON.stringify(body) }\n119: \t\t);\n120: \n121: \t\treturn Promise.resolve(res.ok);\n122: \t}\n123: \n124: \tasync post(endpoint: string, body: FormData | object): Promise<PostResponse | null> {\n125: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n126: \t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n127: \t\t\theaders: typeof body === 'object' ? this.getApiHeaderWithBody() : this.getApiHeader(),\n128: \t\t\tbody: typeof body === 'object' ? JSON.stringify(body) : body\n129: \t\t});\n130: \n131: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n132: \t}\n133: \n134: \tasync postRaw<T = object>(endpoint: string, body: FormData | object): Promise<T> {\n135: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n136: \t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n137: \t\t\theaders: typeof body === 'object' ? this.getApiHeaderWithBody() : this.getApiHeader(),\n138: \t\t\tbody: typeof body === 'object' ? JSON.stringify(body) : body\n139: \t\t});\n140: \n141: \t\treturn await res.json() as Promise<T>;\n142: \t}\n143: \n144: \tasync put(endpoint: string, body: FormData | object): Promise<boolean> {\n145: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n146: \t\t\tmethod: 'PUT',\n147: \t\t\theaders: typeof body === 'object' ? this.getApiHeaderWithBody() : this.getApiHeader(),\n148: \t\t\tbody: typeof body === 'object' ? JSON.stringify(body) : body\n149: \t\t});\n150: \n151: \t\treturn res.ok;\n152: \t}\n153: \n154: \tasync postFormData(endpoint: string, body: FormData): Promise<boolean> {\n155: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n156: \t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n157: \t\t\theaders: this.getAuthHeaderOnly(),\n158: \t\t\tbody: body\n159: \t\t});\n160: \n161: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : false;\n162: \t}\n163: \n164: \tasync uploadFile(endpoint: string, id: string, body: FormData): Promise<CreateResponse | null> {\n165: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint.replace('%s', id), {\n166: \t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n167: \t\t\theaders: this.getAuthHeaderOnly(),\n168: \t\t\tbody\n169: \t\t});\n170: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n171: \t}\n172: \n173: \tasync image(endpoint: string): Promise<Blob | null> {\n174: \t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, { headers: this.getApiHeader() });\n175: \t\treturn res.ok ? await res.blob() : null;\n176: \t}\n177: \n178: \tprivate getAuthHeaderOnly(): HeadersInit {\n179: \t\treturn { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + this.authToken };\n180: \t}\n181: \n182: \tprivate getApiHeader(): HeadersInit {\n183: \t\tif (!this.authToken) {\n184: \t\t\treturn { Accept: 'application/json' };\n185: \t\t}\n186: \n187: \t\treturn { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + this.authToken, Accept: 'application/json' };\n188: \t}\n189: \n190: \tprivate getApiHeaderWithBody(): HeadersInit {\n191: \t\tif (!this.authToken) {\n192: \t\t\treturn { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json' };\n193: \t\t}\n194: \n195: \t\treturn {\n196: \t\t\tAuthorization: 'Bearer ' + this.authToken,\n197: \t\t\t'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n198: \t\t\tAccept: 'application/json'\n199: \t\t};\n200: \t}\n201: }\n\n(End of file - total 201 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import type { CreateResponse, GetResponse, ListResponse, PostResponse } from '$lib/types/api';\nimport { apiRoutes } from '$lib/config/apiRoutes';\n\n// Endpoints where a 401 is a legitimate, expected auth failure (bad credentials,\n// expired refresh token, failed passkey authentication) rather than a stale\n// session. Recovery must never run for these, otherwise a failed login would\n// trigger a refresh/logout loop.\nconst AUTH_ENDPOINTS: string[] = [\n\tapiRoutes.auth.login,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.refresh,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.register,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.verify,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.forgotPassword,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.resetPassword,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.passkeys.authenticateOptions,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.passkeys.authenticate\n];\n\nexport default class ApiService {\n\tauthToken: string | null = null;","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/src/lib/services/ApiService.ts","text":"import type { CreateResponse, GetResponse, ListResponse, PostResponse } from '$lib/types/api';\nimport { apiRoutes } from '$lib/config/apiRoutes';\n\n// Endpoints where a 401 is a legitimate, expected auth failure (bad credentials,\n// expired refresh token, failed passkey authentication) rather than a stale\n// session. Recovery must never run for these, otherwise a failed login would\n// trigger a refresh/logout loop.\nconst AUTH_ENDPOINTS: string[] = [\n\tapiRoutes.auth.login,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.refresh,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.register,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.verify,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.forgotPassword,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.resetPassword,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.passkeys.authenticateOptions,\n\tapiRoutes.auth.passkeys.authenticate\n];\n\nexport default class ApiService {\n\tauthToken: string | null = null;\n\tprivate unauthorizedHandler: (() => Promise<boolean>) | null = null;\n\n\tconstructor(authToken: string | null = null) {\n\t\tthis.authToken = authToken;\n\t}\n\n\tupdateAuthToken(authToken: string | null): void {\n\t\tthis.authToken = authToken;\n\t}\n\n\t// The owner of the session (Auth) registers a single recovery routine here.\n\t// It is expected to adopt a token refreshed by another tab, or refresh this\n\t// session, and return true when a retry with a fresh token makes sense.\n\tsetUnauthorizedHandler(handler: () => Promise<boolean>): void {\n\t\tthis.unauthorizedHandler = handler;\n\t}\n\n\tprivate isAuthEndpoint(endpoint: string): boolean {\n\t\treturn AUTH_ENDPOINTS.some((authEndpoint) => endpoint.startsWith(authEndpoint));\n\t}\n\n\t// Runs a request; on a 401 from a non-auth endpoint asks the session owner\n\t// to recover and, if it did, retries the same request exactly once with the\n\t// current token. Network errors (a rejected fetch) propagate untouched — they\n\t// are transient and must never trigger recovery/logout.\n\tprivate async fetchWithRecovery(endpoint: string, init: RequestInit): Promise<Response> {\n\t\tconst res = await fetch(endpoint, init);\n\n\t\tif (res.status !== 401 || !this.unauthorizedHandler || this.isAuthEndpoint(endpoint)) {\n\t\t\treturn res;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tconst recovered = await this.unauthorizedHandler();\n\t\tif (!recovered) return res;\n\n\t\tconst headers = { ...(init.headers as Record<string, string>) };\n\t\tif (this.authToken) {\n\t\t\theaders['Authorization'] = 'Bearer ' + this.authToken;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tdelete headers['Authorization'];\n\t\t}\n\n\t\treturn fetch(endpoint, { ...init, headers });\n\t}\n\n\tasync list(endpoint: string): Promise<ListResponse | null> {\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, { headers: this.getApiHeader() });\n\t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n\t}\n\n\tasync get(endpoint: string, id: string | number | null): Promise<GetResponse | null> {\n\t\tif (typeof id === 'string') {\n\t\t\tendpoint = endpoint.replace('%s', id);\n\t\t} else if (typeof id === 'number') {\n\t\t\tendpoint = endpoint.replace('%d', id.toString());\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, { headers: this.getApiHeader() });\n\t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n\t}\n\n\tasync create(endpoint: string, body: object): Promise<CreateResponse | null> {\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n\t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n\t\t\theaders: this.getApiHeaderWithBody(),\n\t\t\tbody: JSON.stringify(body)\n\t\t});\n\n\t\treturn res.ok ? await res.json() : null;\n\t}\n\n\tasync createWithStatus(endpoint: string, body: object): Promise<{ ok: boolean; status: number }> {\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n\t\t\tmethod: 'POST',\n\t\t\theaders: this.getApiHeaderWithBody(),\n\t\t\tbody: JSON.stringify(body)\n\t\t});\n\n\t\treturn { ok: res.ok, status: res.status };\n\t}\n\n\tasync delete(endpoint: string, id: string | number): Promise<boolean> {\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(\n\t\t\ttypeof id === 'string'\n\t\t\t\t? endpoint.replace('%s', id)\n\t\t\t\t: endpoint.replace('%d', id.toString()),\n\t\t\t{ method: 'DELETE', headers: this.getApiHeader() }\n\t\t);\n\n\t\treturn Promise.resolve(res.ok);\n\t}\n\n\tasync update(endpoint: string, id: string | number, body: object): Promise<boolean> {\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(\n\t\t\ttypeof id === 'string'\n\t\t\t\t? endpoint.replace('%s', id)\n\t\t\t\t: endpoint.replace('%d', id.toString()),\n\t\t\t{ method: 'PUT', headers: this.getApiHeaderWithBody(), body: JSON.stringify(body) }\n\t\t);\n\n\t\treturn Promise.resolve(res.ok);\n\t}\n\n\tasync post(endpoint: string, body: FormData | object): Promise<PostResponse | null> {\n\t\tconst res = await this.fetchWithRecovery(endpoint, {\n\t\t