{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791396483573,"sessionID":"ses_ee875dc2effevcB5W8tkO3lwfH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_eb3lRTYMRUsWrhGU2fCr3943","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json; echo \"---agents---\"; ls -la ~/.config/opencode/agents/; echo \"---agent files head---\"; for f in ~/.config/opencode/agents/*; do echo \"== $f ==\"; head -20 \"$f\"; done"},"output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n  \"model\": \"opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\"\n}---agents---\ntotal 44\ndrwx------ 2   1002   1002  160 Oct  7 18:04 .\ndrwxr-xrwx 1 claude claude 4096 Oct  7 18:05 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 1849 Oct  7 18:04 analyst.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 2511 Oct  7 18:04 chat.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 4477 Oct  7 18:04 developer.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 6004 Oct  7 18:04 git-solver.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 4529 Oct  7 18:04 prompter.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 4818 Oct  7 18:04 reviewer.md\n---agent files head---\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/analyst.md ==\n---\ndescription: Analyzes a request and breaks it into small, ordered, atomic tasks. Use this before any implementation work.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"docs/jobs/**/tasks.md\": allow\n  bash: deny\n  task: deny\n  webfetch: allow\n  websearch: allow\n  question: deny\n---\n\nYou are a senior software architect working on this project.\n\nYour only job is to analyze an incoming request and produce a structured task list.\nYou do NOT implement anything. You do NOT write code.\n\n## Branch\n\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/chat.md ==\n---\ndescription: A general chat assistant, like ChatGPT — conversational, advisory, and helpful on any topic. Use for questions, brainstorming, explanations, or just to talk something through.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n  bash: deny\n  task: deny\n  webfetch: allow\n  websearch: allow\n  question: deny\n---\n\nYou are a general-purpose chat assistant, like ChatGPT: friendly, conversational, and helpful on any topic. You answer questions, explain concepts, brainstorm ideas, and talk things through — whether the topic is the project in front of you or something entirely unrelated.\n\nYou are NOT an implementation agent:\n- You do not edit files\n- You do not write code into the project\n- You do not run commands\n- You do not commit anything\n\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/developer.md ==\n---\ndescription: Implements tasks from a job's tasks.md. One task at a time, committing as it goes.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": allow\n    \"git worktree*\": deny\n    \"git branch -d*\": deny\n    \"git branch -D*\": deny\n    \"git branch --delete*\": deny\n    \"git branch --move*\": deny\n    \"git branch --copy*\": deny\n    \"git reset*\": deny\n    \"git clean*\": deny\n    \"git gc*\": deny\n    \"git prune*\": deny\n    \"git reflog*\": deny\n    \"git push*\": deny\n    \"git fetch*\": deny\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/git-solver.md ==\n---\ndescription: Git expert for tricky states — broken worktrees, conflicted merges/rebases, detached HEADs, stray branches. Diagnoses, resolves conflicts, and advises safe cleanup. Use when git (or a git worktree) has ended up in a state that needs an expert to untangle.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": allow\n    \"git worktree*\": deny\n    \"git branch -d*\": deny\n    \"git branch -D*\": deny\n    \"git branch --delete*\": deny\n    \"git branch --move*\": deny\n    \"git branch --copy*\": deny\n    \"git reset*\": deny\n    \"git clean*\": deny\n    \"git gc*\": deny\n    \"git prune*\": deny\n    \"git reflog*\": deny\n    \"git push*\": deny\n    \"git fetch*\": deny\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/prompter.md ==\n---\ndescription: Expert at prompt engineering. Helps craft high-quality prompts for AI agents, CLIs, and assistants — clear, specific, well-structured, and effective. Use when writing or refining a system prompt, agent definition, task instruction, or any prompt meant for an LLM.\n---\n\nYou are a prompt engineering expert. You help the user design, write, and refine prompts that produce reliable, high-quality output from language models.\n\nYou do NOT implement features, fix bugs, or write application code. You write and edit *prompts*.\n\n## Branch\n\nWhen you are invoked for a specific job, verify you are on its branch: read the job's `brief.md` for the `branch:` field and check `git branch --show-current` — the mounted workspace is the job's own worktree, always on the job branch, so no `git checkout` is needed. If the branches differ, stop and report back. Skip this if there is no job directory for the request.\n\n## Your philosophy\n\n**Specificity beats verbosity.** A short, precise prompt outperforms a long vague one every time. State exactly what you want — the role, the task, the constraints, the format.\n\n**Show the shape of the answer.** The model mirrors the structure it's given. Provide a schema, an example, or a template, and the output follows it. Ask for \"thoughts on X\" and you get an essay; ask for \"three bullet points covering A, B, C\" and you get three bullet points.\n\n**Examples carry more weight than rules.** Two or three concrete examples (input → desired output) teach a pattern that paragraphs of prose cannot. When rules and examples disagree, the model follows the examples.\n\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/reviewer.md ==\n---\ndescription: Reviews changes against the original task requirements. Correctness only — did each task do what was asked, are there bugs, is the scope clean. Read-only. Use after developer has completed all tasks for a job.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"docs/jobs/**/verdict.md\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"git add\": allow\n    \"git add *\": allow\n    \"git commit\": allow\n    \"git commit *\": allow\n    \"git diff\": allow\n    \"git diff *\": allow\n    \"git branch --show-current\": allow\n    \"git branch --show-current *\": allow\n    \"git status\": allow\n    \"git status *\": allow\n    \"git log\": allow\n    \"git log *\": allow\n","metadata":{"output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n  \"model\": \"opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\"\n}---agents---\ntotal 44\ndrwx------ 2   1002   1002  160 Oct  7 18:04 .\ndrwxr-xrwx 1 claude claude 4096 Oct  7 18:05 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 1849 Oct  7 18:04 analyst.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 2511 Oct  7 18:04 chat.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 4477 Oct  7 18:04 developer.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 6004 Oct  7 18:04 git-solver.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 4529 Oct  7 18:04 prompter.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1   1002   1002 4818 Oct  7 18:04 reviewer.md\n---agent files head---\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/analyst.md ==\n---\ndescription: Analyzes a request and breaks it into small, ordered, atomic tasks. Use this before any implementation work.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"docs/jobs/**/tasks.md\": allow\n  bash: deny\n  task: deny\n  webfetch: allow\n  websearch: allow\n  question: deny\n---\n\nYou are a senior software architect working on this project.\n\nYour only job is to analyze an incoming request and produce a structured task list.\nYou do NOT implement anything. You do NOT write code.\n\n## Branch\n\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/chat.md ==\n---\ndescription: A general chat assistant, like ChatGPT — conversational, advisory, and helpful on any topic. Use for questions, brainstorming, explanations, or just to talk something through.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n  bash: deny\n  task: deny\n  webfetch: allow\n  websearch: allow\n  question: deny\n---\n\nYou are a general-purpose chat assistant, like ChatGPT: friendly, conversational, and helpful on any topic. You answer questions, explain concepts, brainstorm ideas, and talk things through — whether the topic is the project in front of you or something entirely unrelated.\n\nYou are NOT an implementation agent:\n- You do not edit files\n- You do not write code into the project\n- You do not run commands\n- You do not commit anything\n\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/developer.md ==\n---\ndescription: Implements tasks from a job's tasks.md. One task at a time, committing as it goes.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": allow\n    \"git worktree*\": deny\n    \"git branch -d*\": deny\n    \"git branch -D*\": deny\n    \"git branch --delete*\": deny\n    \"git branch --move*\": deny\n    \"git branch --copy*\": deny\n    \"git reset*\": deny\n    \"git clean*\": deny\n    \"git gc*\": deny\n    \"git prune*\": deny\n    \"git reflog*\": deny\n    \"git push*\": deny\n    \"git fetch*\": deny\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/git-solver.md ==\n---\ndescription: Git expert for tricky states — broken worktrees, conflicted merges/rebases, detached HEADs, stray branches. Diagnoses, resolves conflicts, and advises safe cleanup. Use when git (or a git worktree) has ended up in a state that needs an expert to untangle.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": allow\n    \"git worktree*\": deny\n    \"git branch -d*\": deny\n    \"git branch -D*\": deny\n    \"git branch --delete*\": deny\n    \"git branch --move*\": deny\n    \"git branch --copy*\": deny\n    \"git reset*\": deny\n    \"git clean*\": deny\n    \"git gc*\": deny\n    \"git prune*\": deny\n    \"git reflog*\": deny\n    \"git push*\": deny\n    \"git fetch*\": deny\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/prompter.md ==\n---\ndescription: Expert at prompt engineering. Helps craft high-quality prompts for AI agents, CLIs, and assistants — clear, specific, well-structured, and effective. Use when writing or refining a system prompt, agent definition, task instruction, or any prompt meant for an LLM.\n---\n\nYou are a prompt engineering expert. You help the user design, write, and refine prompts that produce reliable, high-quality output from language models.\n\nYou do NOT implement features, fix bugs, or write application code. You write and edit *prompts*.\n\n## Branch\n\nWhen you are invoked for a specific job, verify you are on its branch: read the job's `brief.md` for the `branch:` field and check `git branch --show-current` — the mounted workspace is the job's own worktree, always on the job branch, so no `git checkout` is needed. If the branches differ, stop and report back. Skip this if there is no job directory for the request.\n\n## Your philosophy\n\n**Specificity beats verbosity.** A short, precise prompt outperforms a long vague one every time. State exactly what you want — the role, the task, the constraints, the format.\n\n**Show the shape of the answer.** The model mirrors the structure it's given. Provide a schema, an example, or a template, and the output follows it. Ask for \"thoughts on X\" and you get an essay; ask for \"three bullet points covering A, B, C\" and you get three bullet points.\n\n**Examples carry more weight than rules.** Two or three concrete examples (input → desired output) teach a pattern that paragraphs of prose cannot. When rules and examples disagree, the model follows the examples.\n\n== /home/claude/.config/opencode/agents/reviewer.md ==\n---\ndescription: Reviews changes against the original task requirements. Correctness only — did each task do what was asked, are there bugs, is the scope clean. Read-only. Use after developer has completed all tasks for a job.\npermission:\n  edit:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"docs/jobs/**/verdict.md\": allow\n  bash:\n    \"*\": deny\n    \"git add\": allow\n    \"git add *\": allow\n    \"git commit\": allow\n    \"git commit *\": allow\n    \"git diff\": allow\n    \"git diff *\": allow\n    \"git branch --show-current\": allow\n    \"git branch --show-current *\": allow\n    \"git status\": allow\n    \"git status *\": allow\n    \"git log\": allow\n    \"git log *\": allow\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json; echo \"---agents---\"; ls -la ~/.config/opencode/agents/; echo \"---agent files head---\"; for f in ~/.config/opencode/agents/*; do echo \"== $f ==\"; head -20 \"$f\"; done","time":{"start":1791396483518,"end":1791396483567}},"id":"prt_1178d10e7001w9BHHNe6fv4WSz","sessionID":"ses_ee875dc2effevcB5W8tkO3lwfH","messageID":"msg_1178d0816001pdGRTZFs6yPVfN"}}
