{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402428266,"sessionID":"ses_ee819e651ffeBlXO03MlJMmmql","part":{"id":"prt_117e7bfe70016iJiE68YayGTGv","messageID":"msg_117e7b4de001jeJwToVpzFtSN0","sessionID":"ses_ee819e651ffeBlXO03MlJMmmql","type":"text","text":"The worktree is clean and the job is fully implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe job at `docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away` was already fully implemented and committed by prior developer sessions on the correct branch (`feature/cover_reload-after-time-away`). I verified the state rather than redoing work:\n\n**Verification performed**\n- Branch matches `brief.md` ✓\n- All 7 tasks present in source:\n  - **TASK-1** — only `Auth` constructs an `ApiService`; 27 state stores reference `auth.apiService`; logout clears the shared token.\n  - **TASK-2** — `Auth` session monitor (`visibilitychange` + `online` + hourly interval, `browser`-guarded, interval paused while hidden, single-flight `refresh()`).\n  - **TASK-3** — `ApiService.fetchWithRecovery` 401 ladder, auth-endpoint bypass list, adopt-external-session → refresh → last-resort logout, network errors never log out.\n  - **TASK-4** — `Notes` surfaces failures via notifications and retains modal input; i18n keys present in all four languages and `translation.ts`.\n  - **TASK-5** — `+layout.svelte` reactive `$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` with redirect + session-expired notice.\n  - **TASK-6** — profile-image audit documented (keep — covers a distinct broken-image-fetch mode).\n  - **TASK-7** — verification documented in `implementation.md`.\n- `npm run check` → **0 errors, 0 warnings**\n- Focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`, `AuthTokenFlow`, `Notes`) → **80/80 pass**\n- `npm test` → **715 passed / 716**, the single failure being the pre-existing, unrelated `StatisticWidget` component test (untouched by this branch)\n\n**Changes made this session**\n- No source changes were needed. Committed the harness-owned `session.log`/`tokens.json` as `[cover] chore: finalize worktree (sessio