{"type":"text","timestamp":1791402716475,"sessionID":"ses_ee8166052ffe61W0Zf1odObwJ4","part":{"id":"prt_117ebf9dc001VkxbwRxdrT2PJ1","messageID":"msg_117ebe7a1001jyOacigMW4KPta","sessionID":"ses_ee8166052ffe61W0Zf1odObwJ4","type":"text","text":"The job at `docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away` is **already fully implemented and verified** on branch `feature/cover_reload-after-time-away` (matches `brief.md`). I reviewed the state rather than re-implementing, and confirmed everything:\n\n## What exists (all 7 tasks done, committed)\n\n- **TASK-1** — all 27 state stores now share `Auth`'s single `ApiService` instance (`this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`; grep confirms the only `new ApiService(...)` left in `src/lib/state/` is inside `Auth` itself). `logout()`/`clear()` nulls the token on the shared instance.\n- **TASK-2** — `Auth` re-validates the session on `visibilitychange` → visible, `online`, and an hourly interval while visible (`validateSession()`: local `expires_at` comparison → single-flight `refresh()` → `loadAdditionalData()`; definitive rejection → logout).\n- **TASK-3** — `ApiService.fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request method) runs the 401 recovery ladder: adopt fresher persisted token from another tab → single-flight refresh → retry exactly once → logout only on definitive refresh rejection. `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list prevents login/refresh/passkey endpoints from triggering recovery; network errors propagate untouched.\n- **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()`/`createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` (translation-aware `notes.create_error` / `notes.create_folder_error`) and keep the modal + input on failure; `notes/+layout.svelte` no longer optimistically closes the modal. i18n keys added to `en/de/es/fr` + `translation.ts`.\n- **TASK-5** — `+layout.svelte` has a reactive `$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` that redirects to login/setup with an `auth.session_expired` notice on mid-session logout, without fighting the `onMount` guard or auth/setup routes.\n- **TASK-6** — audited: the earlier profile-image fix (service-worker same-origin GET guard + `NavProfileEntry` retry/letter fallback) covers a distinct failure mode (broken in-session cross-origin image fetch) and is *not* redundant; kept with written justification.\n- **TASK-7** — verification documented in `implementation.md`, including the two open backend facts (refresh-grace window, token revocation on rotation) left as empirical probes with the implementation deliberately agnostic.\n\n## My independent re-verification (this session, node 22)\n\n- `npm run check` → **0 errors / 0 warnings**\n- `npm test` → **715 passed / 716**; the single failure is the pre-existing unrelated `StatisticWidget` component test (test + component untouched by this branch, confirmed via `git diff 22c5a68 HEAD`)\n- ESLint → **exit 0** on every changed source/test file\n- Reviewed the actual `ApiService`/`Auth`/`notes` diffs vs. base `22c5a68` — logic matches the task specs\n\n`implementation.md` is already written and committed; no code changes were needed. I committed the harness-owned session artifacts to leave the worktree as clean as possible — note the harness continuously appends to `session.log`, so a residual one-line dirty state there may reappear after this session ends (it is captured at `mg done` regardless).","time":{"start":1791402703324,"end":1791402716464}}}
