{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791403392628,"sessionID":"ses_ee80996c5ffelQOCGEKSYA3TR6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_WqyRk4WW5BTLi6zVNRFg6387","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: reload after time away\n2: \n3: id: cover\n4: status: open\n5: analyst:\n6: date: 2026-08-19\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Diagnosis\n11: \n12: The session is validated exactly once, at app boot:\n13: \n14: - `Auth` (constructor → `load()`) checks `authToken.expires_at`, refreshes only if\n15:   within 5 days (web) / 14 days (native), then fetches `/users/me`. Nothing ever\n16:   re-runs this while the app stays open — no timer, no `visibilitychange` hook.\n17: - Every feature store snapshots the token at construction\n18:   (`new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`), and `Auth.refresh()` only updates\n19:   Auth's own `ApiService` instance. A refreshed token never reaches the stores.\n20: - `ApiService` swallows every non-ok response (`res.ok ? … : null/false`): no 401\n21:   handling, no retry, no logout, no user feedback.\n22: \n23: So a permanently-open tab drifts into a zombie state: `loggedIn === true` in\n24: memory, token expired/invalid → all API calls fail silently (`Notes.create()`\n25: returns `null` and the modal just closes — \"nothing happens\"; user data incl.\n26: `profile.profile_image_path` is never re-fetched). A hard reload re-runs\n27: `Auth.load()` (expiry check → refresh → `loadAdditionalData()`), which is why\n28: reloading fixes everything.\n29: \n30: The earlier profile-image fix (re-fetching `/users/me` via `loadAdditionalData()`\n31: + `save()`) most likely addressed a symptom of this same root cause; with a\n32: proper resume-driven session check it is probably redundant — audited in TASK-6.\n33: \n34: Out of scope: service worker changes (it already skips API calls), backend\n35: token TTL changes, refactoring all stores to a shared ApiService beyond what\n36: token propagation requires.\n37: \n38: ## Task breakdown\n39: \n40: TASK-1 (decided: Option B): Share Auth's `ApiService` instance across stores.\n41: `Auth` already owns an `ApiService` and keeps its token current on\n42: login/refresh; replace each store's `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`\n43: with `this.auth.apiService` (one mechanical line per store) so a runtime\n44: refresh reaches every request automatically. `logout()` must clear the token on\n45: that shared instance so no store keeps sending the old token. Do not touch\n46: unrelated store logic.\n47: files: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, plus the one-line constructor change in\n48: src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts (~36 stores)\n49: depends: none\n50: risk: medium — every API call now goes through one shared instance; the change\n51: is mechanical per store and covered by `npm run check`.\n52: \n53: TASK-2: Re-validate the session when the app is used again after time away:\n54: on `visibilitychange` → visible (and `online`), plus a low-frequency interval\n55: while visible (e.g. hourly), check `expires_at` — expired → logout; within\n56: refresh threshold → `refresh()` (single-flight: never two concurrent refreshes);\n57: then `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user incl. profile image\n58: path. Guard all listener registration with `browser` (no SSR access to\n59: `document`). Follow the existing `UserNotifications` pattern\n60: (`visibilitychange` + interval, interval stopped while hidden). The routine\n61: check is a local date comparison — no network unless action is needed.\n62: files: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts\n63: depends: TASK-1\n64: risk: medium — new lifecycle listeners and async races; must not double-refresh,\n65: must behave sanely on the desktop/mobile shells (app resume vs. tab visibility).\n66: \n67: TASK-3: Global 401 recovery in `ApiService` — logout strictly as the last\n68: resort. On a 401 from a non-auth endpoint, run a recovery ladder:\n69: (a) re-read the persisted auth from localStorage — if another tab refreshed\n70: the token (multi-tab staleness), adopt it and retry the request (covers\n71: \"stale token although user is still authed\"); (b) otherwise single-flight\n72: `refresh()` and retry the original request exactly once with the new token;\n73: (c) only log out (with UI notification + redirect via TASK-5) if the refresh\n74: itself fails with a definitive auth rejection. Network errors (fetch\n75: rejection / offline) must NOT log out — they are transient and Layer 2\n76: re-checks on `online`. Must explicitly bypass the auth endpoints\n77: (`auth.login`, `auth.refresh`, forgot/reset password, passkey authenticate) —\n78: a failed login legitimately returns 401 and must not trigger recovery. Never\n79: retry a request more than once. New user-visible strings must be added to all\n80: four i18n files.\n81: files: src/lib/services/ApiService.ts, src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts,\n82: src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n83: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n84: risk: high — retry-on-401 logic can loop or misfire; several endpoints return\n85: 401 for normal reasons; `postRaw` parses error bodies and needs care.\n86: \n87: TASK-4: Stop swallowing failed mutations for the reported symptom: surface\n88: `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures via `UiNotifications.error()`\n89: (translation-aware), keeping the user's input in the modal instead of\n90: discarding it. Do not refactor other stores in this job.\n91: files: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts,\n92: src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n93: depends: TASK-3 (so 401s are recovered rather than toasted twice)\n94: risk: low — small, local change; i18n sync is enforced by `npm run check`.\n95: \n96: TASK-5: Make the root layout react to a mid-session logout: the auth guard in\n97: `+layout.svelte` only runs in `onMount`, so `loggedIn` flipping to false after\n98: TASK-2/TASK-3 leaves the user on a dead page. Add a reactive guard (e.g.\n99: `$effect` on `auth.loggedIn`) that redirects to login, without fighting the\n100: existing onMount guard or triggering on auth/setup routes.\n101: files: src/routes/+layout.svelte\n102: depends: TASK-2, TASK-3\n103: risk: low-medium — navigation side effects; must not redirect-loop.\n104: \n105: TASK-6: Audit the previous profile-image fix for redundancy: with resume-driven\n106: `loadAdditionalData()` in place, check whether the earlier change (re-fetch of\n107: `/users/me` after login/`load()`, `profileCache`) still guards a distinct\n108: scenario (e.g. image re-upload changing the storage path, cache busting) and\n109: keep or remove it with a written justification in implementation.md.\n110: files: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte,\n111: src/routes/profile/+page.svelte\n112: depends: TASK-2\n113: risk: low-medium — removing it without confirming the covered scenario could\n114: re-break the profile image.\n115: \n116: TASK-7: Verify: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`; manually simulate\n117: the stale session (dev API with short token TTL or hand-edited `auth` localStorage\n118: entry: (a) expired token + resume from background → refreshed-and-recovered if\n119: the backend honors a grace window, otherwise clean logout — determine which;\n120: (b) near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, notes create works; (c) invalid\n121: token server-side → 401 recovery ladder incl. localStorage adoption for the\n122: multi-tab case; (d) offline/fetch-rejection → no logout, transient only).\n123: Deduced from the client (single bearer token, refresh authenticates with the\n124: current token, empty body): the two open backend facts — (1) does refresh\n125: accept an already-expired token, (2) is the old token revoked on rotation —\n126: are to be probed empirically (curl dev API) and recorded here; the\n127: implementation is deliberately agnostic to both (see recovery ladder), they\n128: only pin down expected outcomes for (a) and (c). Document steps/results in\n129: implementation.md.\n130: files: docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md\n131: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6\n132: risk: low — verification only; no component-test infra exists, so manual steps\n133: are required.\n\n(End of file - total 133 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-08-19\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe session is validated exactly once, at app boot:\n\n- `Auth` (constructor → `load()`) checks `authToken.expires_at`, refreshes only if\n  within 5 days (web) / 14 days (native), then fetches `/users/me`. Nothing ever\n  re-runs this while the app stays open — no timer, no `visibilitychange` hook.\n- Every feature store snapshots the token at construction\n  (`new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`), and `Auth.refresh()` only updates\n  Auth's own `ApiService` instance. A refreshed token never reaches the stores.\n- `ApiService` swallows every non-ok response (`res.ok ? … : null/false`): no 401","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-08-19\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe session is validated exactly once, at app boot:\n\n- `Auth` (constructor → `load()`) checks `authToken.expires_at`, refreshes only if\n  within 5 days (web) / 14 days (native), then fetches `/users/me`. Nothing ever\n  re-runs this while the app stays open — no timer, no `visibilitychange` hook.\n- Every feature store snapshots the token at construction\n  (`new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`), and `Auth.refresh()` only updates\n  Auth's own `ApiService` instance. A refreshed token never reaches the stores.\n- `ApiService` swallows every non-ok response (`res.ok ? … : null/false`): no 401\n  handling, no retry, no logout, no user feedback.\n\nSo a permanently-open tab drifts into a zombie state: `loggedIn === true` in\nmemory, token expired/invalid → all API calls fail silently (`Notes.create()`\nreturns `null` and the modal just closes — \"nothing happens\"; user data incl.\n`profile.profile_image_path` is never re-fetched). A hard reload re-runs\n`Auth.load()` (expiry check → refresh → `loadAdditionalData()`), which is why\nreloading fixes everything.\n\nThe earlier profile-image fix (re-fetching `/users/me` via `loadAdditionalData()`\n+ `save()`) most likely addressed a symptom of this same root cause; with a\nproper resume-driven session check it is probably redundant — audited in TASK-6.\n\nOut of scope: service worker changes (it already skips API calls), backend\ntoken TTL changes, refactoring all stores to a shared ApiService beyond what\ntoken propagation requires.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1 (decided: Option B): Share Auth's `ApiService` instance across stores.\n`Auth` already owns an `ApiService` and keeps its token current on\nlogin/refresh; replace each store's `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`\nwith `this.auth.apiService` (one mechanical line per store) so a runtime\nrefresh reaches every request automatically. `logout()` must clear the token on\nthat shared instance so no store keeps sending the old token. Do not touch\nunrelated store logic.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, plus the one-line constructor change in\nsrc/lib/state/*.svelte.ts (~36 stores)\ndepends: none\nrisk: medium — every API call now goes through one shared instance; the change\nis mechanical per store and covered by `npm run check`.\n\nTASK-2: Re-validate the session when the app is used again after time away:\non `visibilitychange` → visible (and `online`), plus a low-frequency interval\nwhile visible (e.g. hourly), check `expires_at` — expired → logout; within\nrefresh threshold → `refresh()` (single-flight: never two concurrent refreshes);\nthen `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user incl. profile image\npath. Guard all listener registration with `browser` (no SSR access to\n`document`). Follow the existing `UserNotifications` pattern\n(`visibilitychange` + interval, interval stopped while hidden). The routine\ncheck is a local date comparison — no network unless action is needed.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts\ndepends: TASK-1\nrisk: medium — new lifecycle listeners and async races; must not double-refresh,\nmust behave sanely on the desktop/mobile shells (app resume vs. tab visibility).\n\nTASK-3: Global 401 recovery in `ApiService` — logout strictly as the last\nresort. On a 401 from a non-auth endpoint, run a recovery ladder:\n(a) re-read the persisted auth from localStorage — if another tab refreshed\nthe token (multi-tab staleness), adopt it and retry the request (covers\n\"stale token although user is still authed\"); (b) otherwise single-flight\n`refresh()` and retry the original request exactly once with the new token;\n(c) only log out (with UI notification + redirect via TASK-5) if the refresh\nitself fails with a definitive auth rejection. Network errors (fetch\nrejection / offline) must NOT log out — they are transient and Layer 2\nre-checks on `online`. Must explicitly bypass the auth endpoints\n(`auth.login`, `auth.refresh`, forgot/reset password, passkey authenticate) —\na failed login legitimately returns 401 and must not trigger recovery. Never\nretry a request more than once. New user-visible strings must be added to all\nfour i18n files.\nfiles: src/lib/services/ApiService.ts, src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts,\nsrc/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2\nrisk: high — retry-on-401 logic can loop or misfire; several endpoints return\n401 for normal reasons; `postRaw` parses error bodies and needs care.\n\nTASK-4: Stop swallowing failed mutations for the reported symptom: surface\n`Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures via `UiNotifications.error()`\n(translation-aware), keeping the user's input in the modal instead of\ndiscarding it. Do not refactor other stores in this job.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts,\nsrc/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\ndepends: TASK-3 (so 401s are recovered rather than toasted twice)\nrisk: low — small, local change; i18n sync is enforced by `npm run check`.\n\nTASK-5: Make the root layout react to a mid-session logout: the auth guard in\n`+layout.svelte` only runs in `onMount`, so `loggedIn` flipping to false after\nTASK-2/TASK-3 leaves the user on a dead page. Add a reactive guard (e.g.\n`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn`) that redirects to login, without fighting the\nexisting onMount guard or triggering on auth/setup routes.\nfiles: src/routes/+layout.svelte\ndepends: TASK-2, TASK-3\nrisk: low-medium — navigation side effects; must not redirect-loop.\n\nTASK-6: Audit the previous profile-image fix for redundancy: with resume-driven\n`loadAdditionalData()` in place, check whether the earlier change (re-fetch of\n`/users/me` after login/`load()`, `profileCache`) still guards a distinct\nscenario (e.g. image re-upload changing the storage path, cache busting) and\nkeep or remove it with a written justification in implementation.md.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts, src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte,\nsrc/routes/profile/+page.svelte\ndepends: TASK-2\nrisk: low-medium — removing it without confirming the covered scenario could\nre-break the profile image.\n\nTASK-7: Verify: `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`; manually simulate\nthe stale session (dev API with short token TTL or hand-edited `auth` localStorage\nentry: (a) expired token + resume from background → refreshed-and-recovered if\nthe backend honors a grace window, otherwise clean logout — determine which;\n(b) near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, notes create works; (c) invalid\ntoken server-side → 401 recovery ladder incl. localStorage adoption for the\nmulti-tab case; (d) offline/fetch-rejection → no logout, transient only).\nDeduced from the client (single bearer token, refresh authenticates with the\ncurrent token, empty body): the two open backend facts — (1) does refresh\naccept an already-expired token, (2) is the old token revoked on rotation —\nare to be probed empirically (curl dev API) and recorded here; the\nimplementation is deliberately agnostic to both (see recovery ladder), they\nonly pin down expected outcomes for (a) and (c). Document steps/results in\nimplementation.md.\nfiles: docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6\nrisk: low — verification only; no component-test infra exists, so manual steps\nare required.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":133,"totalLines":133,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791403392249,"end":1791403392504}},"id":"prt_117f67cda0014AVwVrjwUPWndN","sessionID":"ses_ee80996c5ffelQOCGEKSYA3TR6","messageID":"msg_117f66f110012dpOqvotV7XXRC"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791403392630,"sessionID":"ses_ee80996c5ffelQOCGEKSYA3TR6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_G6hGGRzbc7WdabBuXh8G7467","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/brief.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief: reload after time away\n2: \n3: status: open\n4: type: feature\n5: id: cover\n6: branch: feature/cover_reload-after-time-away\n7: date: 2026-08-19\n8: author: Leander Muskalla\n9: \n10: ## What\n11: \n12: Previously we had tried to fix a bug where the profile image didn't load. Whatever we did, it wasn't the whole answer.\n13: What I discovered now is that the issue is somewhere deeper. There seems to be the possibility to have the app open, go away, re-open later (maybe even a few days) and the app shows/loads up fine, but the profile image might not load and when I want to add entries (e.g. in the notes section), nothing happens.\n14: I expect this is a stale state where theoretically we had been logged in and had received a valid token, but then that went stale and when we come back without a hard refresh on the page, we're somewhere in between.\n15: Because: when I reload the whole page, therefore reload the whole JS setup, everything is fine after that.\n16: Any ideas on how to solve this cleanly?\n17: Many people have solyto permanently open. So this is a common scenario.\n18: Please also check if our fix to the profile image was therefore unnecessary.\n19: \n20: ## Why\n21: \n22: <!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n23: \n24: ## Out of scope\n25: \n26: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n27: \n28: ## Notes\n29: \n30: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief: reload after time away\n\nstatus: open\ntype: feature\nid: cover\nbranch: feature/cover_reload-after-time-away\ndate: 2026-08-19\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nPreviously we had tried to fix a bug where the profile image didn't load. Whatever we did, it wasn't the whole answer.\nWhat I discovered now is that the issue is somewhere deeper. There seems to be the possibility to have the app open, go away, re-open later (maybe even a few days) and the app shows/loads up fine, but the profile image might not load and when I want to add entries (e.g. in the notes section), nothing happens.\nI expect this is a stale state where theoretically we had been logged in and had received a valid token, but then that went stale and when we come back without a hard refresh on the page, we're somewhere in between.\nBecause: when I reload the whole page, therefore reload the whole JS setup, everything is fine after that.\nAny ideas on how to solve this cleanly?\nMany people have solyto permanently open. So this is a common scenario.\nPlease also check if our fix to the profile image was therefore unnecessary.\n\n## Why","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/brief.md","text":"# Brief: reload after time away\n\nstatus: open\ntype: feature\nid: cover\nbranch: feature/cover_reload-after-time-away\ndate: 2026-08-19\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nPreviously we had tried to fix a bug where the profile image didn't load. Whatever we did, it wasn't the whole answer.\nWhat I discovered now is that the issue is somewhere deeper. There seems to be the possibility to have the app open, go away, re-open later (maybe even a few days) and the app shows/loads up fine, but the profile image might not load and when I want to add entries (e.g. in the notes section), nothing happens.\nI expect this is a stale state where theoretically we had been logged in and had received a valid token, but then that went stale and when we come back without a hard refresh on the page, we're somewhere in between.\nBecause: when I reload the whole page, therefore reload the whole JS setup, everything is fine after that.\nAny ideas on how to solve this cleanly?\nMany people have solyto permanently open. So this is a common scenario.\nPlease also check if our fix to the profile image was therefore unnecessary.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n\n## Notes\n\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":30,"totalLines":30,"truncated":false}},"