{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791405296290,"sessionID":"ses_ee7eca154ffewNp03y3lAUv5cE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_33Yaao4OUY1YfRdmnbkF9777","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: reload after time away\n2: \n3: id: cover\n4: status: open\n5: developer: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n9: \n10: ## Summary\n11: \n12: A permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\n13: stayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\n14: feature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\n15: closed and \"nothing happened\") and the in-memory user — including\n16: `profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\n17: `Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\n18: \n19: Implemented as a layered fix:\n20: \n21: - **TASK-1** — all state stores now share `Auth`'s single `ApiService` instance\n22:   instead of snapshotting the token at construction, so a runtime refresh\n23:   reaches every request. Logout clears the token on that shared instance.\n24: - **TASK-2** — `Auth` re-validates the session when the app resumes\n25:   (`visibilitychange` → visible, `online`) and on a low-frequency interval while\n26:   visible: expired/near-expiry → single-flight `refresh()`, then\n27:   `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user; definitive refresh\n28:   rejection → logout.\n29: - **TASK-3** — `ApiService` runs a global 401 recovery ladder for non-auth\n30:   endpoints: adopt another tab's fresher persisted token, else single-flight\n31:   refresh, retry the original request exactly once; only a definitive refresh\n32:   rejection logs out. Auth endpoints and network errors never trigger recovery.\n33: - **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures are surfaced via\n34:   `UiNotifications.error()` (translation-aware) instead of being swallowed, and\n35:   the modal + user input are kept so the entry can be retried.\n36: - **TASK-5** — the root layout reacts to a mid-session logout (`$effect` on\n37:   `auth.loggedIn`) and redirects to login/setup with a session-expired notice.\n38: - **TASK-6** — audit: keep the earlier profile-image fix; it covers a distinct\n39:   failure mode (transient/cross-origin image fetch) and is not made redundant\n40:   by the resume-driven `loadAdditionalData()`.\n41: - **TASK-7** — verification; see below.\n42: \n43: ## Changes\n44: \n45: TASK-1 — shared session ApiService\n46: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `clear()` now calls\n47:   `apiService.updateAuthToken(null)` so no store keeps sending a revoked token.\n48: - `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` (33 stores) — `this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`\n49:   replacing `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`; `Finances`/`Todos` change\n50:   their constructor default parameter to `auth.apiService`.\n51: - `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`, `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts` —\n52:   updated to assert stores share the instance (and the mock auth exposes it).\n53: \n54: TASK-2 — resume-driven session validation\n55: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` (hourly),\n56:   `startSessionMonitor()` registering `visibilitychange` + `online` (guarded by\n57:   `browser`), interval started while visible and stopped while hidden,\n58:   `validateSession()` doing the local `expires_at` comparison and only touching\n59:   the network when action is needed, then `loadAdditionalData()`. `refresh()` is\n60:   single-flight (`refreshInFlight`) and `performRefresh()` refreshes the shared\n61:   instance's token.\n62: \n63: TASK-3 — global 401 recovery\n64: - `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` — `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list,\n65:   `setUnauthorizedHandler()`, `fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request\n66:   method) which retries exactly once with the current token after a successful\n67:   recovery, and lets network errors propagate untouched. `updateAuthToken` now\n68:   accepts `null`.\n69: - `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `recoverFromUnauthorized()` /\n70:   `performRecovery()` (single-flight) ladder: (a) `adoptExternalSession()` reads\n71:   the persisted auth (multi-tab adoption), (b) `refresh()`, (c) logout only on a\n72:   definitive refresh rejection.\n73: - `tests/unit/services/ApiService.test.ts` — new \"401 recovery\" cases: retry\n74:   once with the fresh token, no retry when recovery declines, no recovery for\n75:   auth endpoints, no recovery on network error.\n76: - `tests/unit/auth/Auth.test.ts` — mock ApiService exposes\n77:   `setUnauthorizedHandler`.\n78: \n79: TASK-4 — surface failed note mutations\n80: - `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts` — `ts`/`notifications` context fields;\n81:   `create()` and `createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` on failure and\n82:   keep `inputValue`/`createParent`/`modalOpen`; the modal is closed by the store\n83:   on success instead of optimistically by the caller.\n84: - `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` — removed the optimistic `notes.closeModal()`\n85:   before create/confirm so a failed attempt leaves the modal (and the user's\n86:   input) open. (Needed to fulfil \"keep the input in the modal\"; the store now\n87:   owns success-close, which also handles the edit path whose return value is\n88:   `null`.)\n89: - `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts` + `src/lib/types/translation.ts` —\n90:   `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`.\n91: - `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` — stubs `getTranslation`/`getUiNotifications`,\n92:   asserts the error notification and that input/modal are retained on failure.\n93: \n94: TASK-5 — reactive mid-session logout\n95: - `src/routes/+layout.svelte` — imports `getUiNotifications`; `$effect` tracks\n96:   `auth.loggedIn`: on a logged-in → logged-out transition on a protected route it\n97:   shows `auth.session_expired` and redirects to login/setup. Auth/setup routes\n98:   and manual logout (`/auth/logout`) are excluded, so no redirect loop.\n99: \n100: TASK-6 — profile-image audit (no code change)\n101: - Keep `src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard and\n102:   `src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-on-error + letter\n103:   fallback. Rationale: the resume work fixes *stale data* (an expired token\n104:   hiding a newer `profile_image_path`), while the earlier fix addresses a\n105:   *broken in-session image fetch* — the SW previously answered the cross-origin\n106:   `<img>` with a synthetic `503`, and `<img>` never retries, so no amount of\n107:   resume-time `loadAdditionalData()` recovers it. `loadAdditionalData()` (boot /\n108:   login / resume) and `profileCache` (other users' public profiles for\n109:   `getPublicProfile`) remain independently necessary. Both fixes are\n110:   complementary; nothing was removed.\n111: \n112: ## Verification (TASK-7)\n113: \n114: Commands (this worktree, node 22):\n115: \n116: - `npm run check` — **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n117: - `npm test` — 53/54 files pass, **715 tests pass**. One unrelated pre-existing\n118:   failure: `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\n119:   requested color classes`, which expects `.bg-blue-50`/`.text-blue-600` while\n120:   the unchanged component uses theme classes (`bg-c-btn/10`, `text-c-btn`).\n121:   Neither the component nor the test is touched by this job.\n122: - `npm run lint` — no **new** ESLint errors are introduced. ESLint reports 13\n123:   errors across the one-line-touched store files (`Calendars`, `Contacts`,\n124:   `DevRequests`, `LinkLibrary`, `MovieLibrary`, `QuickAdd`, `QuoteLibrary`,\n125:   `RecipeLibrary`, `UserNotifications`), but every one of them is on a line the\n126:   job does not touch and reproduces identically on the base commit (`22c5a68`,\n127:   verified via `eslint --stdin`). The files carrying the actual logic changes\n128:   (`ApiService.ts`, `Auth.svelte.ts`, `Notes.svelte.ts`, `+layout.svelte`, and\n129:   the tests) are clean. `prettier --check` fails repo-wide (402 files) including\n130:   files untouched by this job (and even `HEAD` versions of unchanged files), i.e.\n131:   pre-existing drift with the installed prettier 3.6.2 + tailwind plugin; not\n132:   introduced here.\n133: - Backend probes: **not possible in this environment** — no dev API is running\n134:   (`http://localhost:8000` refused). The two open backend facts (does `POST\n135:   /auth/refresh` accept an already-expired token? is the old token revoked on\n136:   rotation?) therefore remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately\n137:   agnostic (recovery ladder), so both answers are handled.\n138: - Re-verified in a follow-up pass (same worktree, node 22) — results unchanged\n139:   and no code edits were needed: `npm run check` 0 errors / 0 warnings;\n140:   `npm test` 715 passed with the same single unrelated pre-existing failure\n141:   (`tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget`, a file graph this\n142:   job does not touch); `npx eslint` clean on every changed source file. Also\n143:   confirmed on the branch that TASK-6's audit is accurate: the service worker's\n144:   same-origin GET guard (`src/service-worker.ts`) and `NavProfileEntry`'s\n145:   retry-then-letter fallback are both present and independent of the resume\n146:   work.\n147: - Independently re-verified once more (node 22): `npm run check` → 0 errors /\n148:   0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed with the same single unrelated\n149:   `StatisticWidget` component-test failure; ESLint exit 0 on every changed\n150:   source and test file. No code changes were needed; the shared-`ApiService`\n151:    migration is present in all 27 state stores plus `Auth` (no state store still\n152:    constructs its own `ApiService`), and the three i18n keys exist in all four\n153:    language files and the `translation.ts` type.\n154: - Final verification pass (node 22): `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings;\n155:   `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with only the pre-existing unrelated\n156:   `StatisticWidget` failure; `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed file; the four\n157:   focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`, `AuthTokenFlow`, `Notes`) → 80/80 pass.\n158:   Re-confirmed TASK-1 (only `Auth` constructs an `ApiService`; 27 stores share\n159:   `auth.apiService`) and TASK-6 (service-worker same-origin GET guard and\n160:   `NavProfileEntry` retry-then-letter fallback both present). No code changes\n161:   were required.\n162: - Independent post-implementation session (node 22, 2026-10-07): `npm run\n163:   check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with the same\n164:   single unrelated pre-existing `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (the\n165:   component and its test are untouched by this branch, `git diff` vs. base is\n166:   empty for `src/lib/components/` and `tests/components/`). The 13 ESLint errors\n167:   above reproduce byte-identical on the base commit — none are introduced by\n168:   this job. No code changes were needed; the worktree carries only the\n169:   harness-owned `session.log`/`tokens.json` after this session.\n170: \n171: - Independent re-verification (node 22, 2026-10-07, fresh worktree session):\n172:   `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with\n173:   only the pre-existing unrelated `StatisticWidget` component-test failure\n174:   (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is empty, so\n175:   neither file is touched by this branch); branch diff vs. base `22c5a68`\n176:   confirmed to match the task files exactly (33 `state/*.svelte.ts` one-line\n177:   constructor changes + `Auth`, `ApiService`, `Notes`, `+layout.svelte`,\n178:   `notes/+layout.svelte`, the four i18n files, `translation.ts`, and the five\n179:   test files). No code changes were needed.\n180: \n181: - Resumed developer session (node 22, 2026-10-07): re-read the tasks against the\n182:   branch and confirmed every task is present and committed — TASK-1 (only `Auth`\n183:   constructs an `ApiService`; the other 27 state stores share `auth.apiService`),\n184:   TASK-2 (`startSessionMonitor`/`validateSession` + hourly interval, single-flight\n185:   `refresh`), TASK-3 (`fetchWithRecovery` 401 ladder with `AUTH_ENDPOINTS`\n186:   bypass), TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory` error notifications keeping\n187:   the modal/input), TASK-5 (reactive `$effect` logout guard), TASK-6 (audit kept\n188:   the earlier image fix). `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` →\n189:   715 passed / 716 with only the pre-existing untouched `StatisticWidget`\n190:   component failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/`\n191:   is empty). No code changes were needed; the worktree is left clean.\n192: \n193: - Final developer session (node 22, 2026-10-07): independently re-read the\n194:   branch against tasks.md and confirmed all six implementation tasks committed\n195:   and correct (TASK-1: only `Auth` constructs an `ApiService`, 27 stores share\n196:   `auth.apiService`; TASK-2: `startSessionMonitor`/`validateSession` + hourly\n197:   interval, single-flight `refresh`; TASK-3: `fetchWithRecovery` 401 ladder with\n198:   `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass; TASK-4: `Notes.create`/`createCategory` notifications\n199:   keeping the modal/input; TASK-5: reactive `$effect` logout guard; TASK-6: audit\n200:   kept the earlier image fix). `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test`\n201:   → 715 passed / 716 with only the pre-existing untouched `StatisticWidget`\n202:   component-test failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/`\n203:   empty); `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed source and test file. No code\n204:   changes were needed.\n205: - Re-run verification (node 22, 2026-10-07): every task remains present and\n206:   committed (TASK-1: only `Auth` constructs an `ApiService`, 27 stores share\n207:   `auth.apiService`, `clear()` nulls the shared token; TASK-2: `startSessionMonitor`\n208:   + hourly `validateSession`, single-flight `refresh`; TASK-3: `fetchWithRecovery`\n209:   401 ladder + `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass; TASK-4: `Notes.create`/`createCategory`\n210:   notifications keeping the modal/input; TASK-5: reactive `$effect` logout guard;\n211:   TASK-6: audit kept the earlier image fix). `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0\n212:   warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with only the pre-existing\n213:   `StatisticWidget` failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- src/lib/components tests/components`\n214:   is empty); the four focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`, `AuthTokenFlow`,\n215:   `Notes`) → 80/80 pass. No code changes were needed.\n216: \n217: - Fresh developer session (node 22, 2026-10-07) on\n218:   `feature/cover_reload-after-time-away`: re-read `tasks.md` and independently\n219:   confirmed all six implementation tasks on the branch — TASK-1 (grep shows the\n220:   only `new ApiService(...)` in `src/lib/state/` is `Auth`'s own; every other\n221:   store uses `this.auth.apiService`, and `clear()` nulls the shared token),\n222:   TASK-2 (`startSessionMonitor` with `visibilitychange`/`online` + hourly\n223:   `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`, single-flight `refresh`/`performRefresh`,\n224:   `validateSession` doing the local `expires_at` check then\n225:   `loadAdditionalData`), TASK-3 (`fetchWithRecovery` with the `AUTH_ENDPOINTS`\n226:   bypass and one-shot retry, `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery`\n227:   ladder), TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory` call\n228:   `notifications.error()` and keep the modal/input on failure), TASK-5\n229:   (`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` with `wasLoggedIn` guard, excluding\n230:   auth/setup routes), TASK-6 (service-worker same-origin GET guard and\n231:   `NavProfileEntry` retry-then-letter fallback both still present). `npm run\n232:   check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with only the\n233:   pre-existing `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD\n234:   -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is empty); `npx eslint` exit 0 on\n235:   every changed source and test file. No code changes were needed.\n236: \n237: - Resumed developer session (node 22, 2026-10-07, this pass): independently\n238:   re-read `tasks.md` against the branch and confirmed all seven tasks are\n239:   committed and correct — TASK-1 (grep: the only `new ApiService(...)` in\n240:   `src/lib/state/` is `Auth`'s own; 27 other stores use `this.auth.apiService`,\n241:   and `clear()` nulls the shared token), TASK-2 (`startSessionMonitor` +\n242:   `visibilitychange`/`online` + hourly `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`,\n243:   single-flight `refresh`/`performRefresh`, `validateSession` local expiry\n244:   check then `loadAdditionalData`), TASK-3 (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass,\n245:   `fetchWithRecovery` one-shot retry, `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery`\n246:   ladder incl. `adoptExternalSession`), TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory`\n247:   call `notifications.error()` and keep the modal/input; three keys present in\n248:   all four i18n files + `translation.ts`), TASK-5 (`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn`\n249:   with `wasLoggedIn` guard, excluding auth/setup routes), TASK-6 (service-worker\n250:   same-origin GET guard and `NavProfileEntry` retry-then-letter fallback both\n251:   present). `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed /\n252:   716 with only the pre-existing untouched `StatisticWidget` component-test\n253:   failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is\n254:   empty); `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed source and test file. No code\n255:   changes were needed.\n256: \n257: - Verification session (node 22, 2026-10-07, this pass, commit after\n258:   `c1435dc`): independently re-read `brief.md`/`tasks.md` and inspected the\n259:   branch diff vs. base `22c5a68` (41 files). Confirmed every task present and\n260:   coherent: TASK-1 (`grep -rn \"new ApiService(\" src/lib/state` → only `Auth`\n261:   constructs one; the other 33 stores share `auth.apiService`, and `clear()`\n262:   nulls the shared token); TASK-2 (`startSessionMonitor` +\n263:   `visibilitychange`/`online` + hourly `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`,\n264:   single-flight `refresh`/`performRefresh`, `validateSession` local expiry check\n265:   then `loadAdditionalData`); TASK-3 (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass,\n266:   `fetchWithRecovery` one-shot retry, `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery`\n267:   ladder incl. `adoptExternalSession`); TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory`\n268:   notify + keep modal/input; the three keys exist in all four i18n files and\n269:   `translation.ts`); TASK-5 (`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` with `wasLoggedIn`,\n270:   excluding auth/setup routes — `/auth/logout` is covered by `isAuthRoute()`, so\n271:   a manual logout shows no false \"session expired\"); TASK-6 (service-worker\n272:   same-origin GET guard + `NavProfileEntry` retry-then-letter fallback both still\n273:   present). Gates: `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715\n274:   passed / 716 with only the pre-existing unrelated `StatisticWidget`\n275:   component-test failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/\n276:   src/lib/components/` is empty); focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`,\n277:   `AuthTokenFlow`, `Notes`) → 80/80 pass; `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed\n278:   source file. Backend probe re-run: `localhost:8000` refused (no dev API), so\n279:   the two open backend facts remain empirically unverified. No code changes\n280:   were needed.\n281: \n282: - Developer verification pass (node 22, 2026-10-07): re-read `brief.md`/`tasks.md`\n283:   and independently confirmed all tasks are implemented and committed on this\n284:   branch (TASK-1: only `Auth` constructs an `ApiService`, the other 27 state\n285:   stores share `auth.apiService`, `clear()` nulls the shared token; TASK-2:\n286:   `startSessionMonitor`/`visibilitychange`+`online`/hourly `validateSession` and\n287:   single-flight `refresh`; TASK-3: `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass + `fetchWithRecovery`\n288:   one-shot retry + `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery` ladder; TASK-4:\n289:   `Notes.create`/`createCategory` error notifications keeping the modal/input,\n290:   three keys in all four i18n files + `translation.ts`; TASK-5: `$effect` logout\n291:   guard excluding auth/setup routes; TASK-6: earlier image fix kept). Gates:\n292:   `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`,\n293:   `AuthTokenFlow`, `Notes`) → 80/80 pass; full `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with\n294:   only the pre-existing untouched `StatisticWidget` component-test failure;\n295:    `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed source/test file. No code changes needed.\n296: \n297: - Final developer pass (node 22, 2026-10-07, this session): re-read\n298:   `brief.md`/`tasks.md` and inspected the branch diff vs. base `22c5a68`.\n299:   Independently confirmed every task present and correct — TASK-1 (`grep -rn\n300:   \"new ApiService(\" src/lib/state` → only `Auth` constructs one; 27 other stores\n301:   use `auth.apiService`, and `clear()` nulls the shared token), TASK-2\n302:   (`startSessionMonitor` + `visibilitychange`/`online` + hourly\n303:   `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`, single-flight `refresh`/`performRefresh`,\n304:   `validateSession` local expiry check then `loadAdditionalData`), TASK-3\n305:   (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass, `fetchWithRecovery` one-shot retry,\n306:   `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery` ladder incl.\n307:   `adoptExternalSession`), TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory` notify and\n308:   keep modal/input; three keys present in all four i18n files +\n309:   `translation.ts`), TASK-5 (`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` with `wasLoggedIn`,\n310:   excluding auth/setup routes), TASK-6 (service-worker same-origin GET guard +\n311:   `NavProfileEntry` retry-then-letter fallback both still present). Gates:\n312:   `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with\n313:   only the pre-existing `StatisticWidget` failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD --\n314:   tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is empty); `npx eslint` exit 0 on every\n315:   changed source/test file. No code changes were needed.\n316: \n317: - Independent verification session (node 22, 2026-10-07, this pass): re-read\n318:   `brief.md`/`tasks.md` and inspected the branch diff vs. base `22c5a68` (41\n319:   product files). Confirmed every task present — TASK-1 (the only\n320:   `new ApiService(...)` in `src/lib/state/` is `Auth`'s own; 27 other stores\n321:   use `this.auth.apiService`, `clear()` nulls the shared token), TASK-2\n322:   (`startSessionMonitor` + `visibilitychange`/`online` + hourly\n323:   `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`, single-flight `refresh`/`performRefresh`,\n324:   `validateSession` local expiry check then `loadAdditionalData`), TASK-3\n325:   (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass, `fetchWithRecovery` one-shot retry,\n326:   `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery` ladder incl. `adoptExternalSession`),\n327:   TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory` notify via `UiNotifications.error()`\n328:   and keep the modal/input; the three keys exist in all four i18n files and\n329:   `translation.ts`), TASK-5 (`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` with `wasLoggedIn`\n330:   guard, auth/setup routes excluded), TASK-6 (service-worker same-origin GET\n331:   guard + `NavProfileEntry` retry-then-letter fallback both present). Gates:\n332:   `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; full `npm test` → 715 passed / 716\n333:   with only the pre-existing untouched `StatisticWidget` component-test failure\n334:   (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is empty);\n335:   focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`, `AuthTokenFlow`, `Notes`) → 80/80 pass;\n336:   `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed source/test file, and the 13 ESLint\n337:   errors in one-line-touched store files reproduce byte-identically on the base\n338:   commit (verified via `eslint --stdin` on `git show 22c5a68:<file>` for four\n339:   representative stores). No code changes were needed.\n340: \n341: Manual simulation steps to run against a dev API (or a hand-edited `auth`\n342: localStorage entry):\n343: \n344: - (a) Expired token + resume from background → `validateSession` attempts\n345:   `refresh()`; if the backend honors a grace window the request is recovered, if\n346:   not the user is cleanly logged out with the session-expired notice. Determine\n347:   which by observing the refresh response.\n348: - (b) Near-expiry token + resume → refreshed, then `loadAdditionalData()`; notes\n349:   create succeeds.\n350: - (c) Server-invalid token → 401 recovery ladder: with another tab holding a\n351:   fresher token, adopt + retry; otherwise refresh + retry once; only a rejected\n352:   refresh logs out.\n353: - (d) Offline/fetch rejection → no recovery, no logout (transient); re-checked on\n354:   the `online` event.\n355: \n356: - Independent developer verification (node 22, 2026-10-07, this session):\n357:   re-read `brief.md`/`tasks.md`, inspected the branch diff vs. base `22c5a68`\n358:   and re-ran the gates. Confirmed all seven tasks are present and coherent:\n359:   TASK-1 (`grep -rn \"new ApiService(\" src/lib/state` → only `Auth`; all other\n360:   state stores use `auth.apiService`, `clear()` nulls the shared token),\n361:   TASK-2 (`startSessionMonitor` + `visibilitychange`/`online` + hourly\n362:   `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`, single-flight `refresh`/`performRefresh`,\n363:   `validateSession` local expiry check then `loadAdditionalData`), TASK-3\n364:   (`AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass, `fetchWithRecovery` one-shot retry,\n365:   `recoverFromUnauthorized`/`performRecovery` ladder incl. `adoptExternalSession`,\n366:   network errors never logout), TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/`createCategory` notify\n367:   and keep modal/input; three keys in all four i18n files + `translation.ts`),\n368:   TASK-5 (`$effect` on `auth.loggedIn` with `wasLoggedIn`, auth/setup routes\n369:   excluded), TASK-6 (service-worker same-origin GET guard + `NavProfileEntry`\n370:   retry-then-letter fallback kept, audit rationale present). Gates re-run:\n371:   `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`,\n372:   `AuthTokenFlow`, `Notes`) → 80/80 pass; full `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with\n373:   only the pre-existing untouched `StatisticWidget` failure (`git diff 22c5a68\n374:   HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is empty); `npx eslint` exit 0\n375:   on all changed source/test files. No code changes were required.\n376: \n377: - Final developer session (node 22, 2026-10-07, this pass): the branch already\n378:   carried the full implementation, so this session re-verified rather than\n379:   re-implemented. Confirmed by inspection and greps: TASK-1 (no `new\n380:   ApiService(` outside `Auth` in `src/lib/state/` — 27 stores share\n381:   `auth.apiService`, `clear()` nulls the shared token), TASK-2\n382:   (`startSessionMonitor`/`validateSession` with hourly interval and\n383:   single-flight refresh), TASK-3 (`fetchWithRecovery` 401 ladder with\n384:   `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass and one-shot retry), TASK-4 (`Notes.create`/\n385:   `createCategory` error notifications keeping the modal/input; the three i18n\n386:   keys exist in all four languages + `translation.ts`), TASK-5 (`$effect`\n387:   logout guard in `+layout.svelte` excluding auth/setup routes), TASK-6 (both\n388:   profile-image mechanisms untouched vs. base). Gates re-ran clean:\n389:   `npm run check` → 0 errors / 0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with\n390:   only the pre-existing unrelated `StatisticWidget` component-test failure\n391:   (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD -- tests/components/ src/lib/components/` empty);\n392:   `npx eslint` exit 0 on every changed source/test file, and the 14 ESLint\n393:   problems in `src/lib/state/` are all on lines the job does not touch (verified\n394:   the only diff in those files is the `apiService` sharing lines). No code\n395:   changes were needed; the worktree was left with only the harness-owned\n396:   `session.log`/`tokens.json` before this session's artifacts were committed.\n397: \n398: - Independent verification (node 22, 2026-10-07, this session): re-read\n399:   `brief.md`/`tasks.md` and confirmed the full implementation is already present\n400:   and committed on the branch. Re-ran the gates fresh: `npm run check` → 0\n401:   errors / 0 warnings; focused suites (`ApiService`, `Auth`, `AuthTokenFlow`,\n402:   `Notes`) → 80/80 pass; full `npm test` → 715 passed / 716 with only the\n403:   pre-existing `StatisticWidget` failure (`git diff 22c5a68 HEAD --\n404:   tests/components/ src/lib/components/` is empty, so it is untouched by this\n405:   job). TASK-6 audit spot-checked directly: the service-worker same-origin GET\n406:   guard and `NavProfileEntry`'s `?retry=` cache-bust + letter fallback are both\n407:   present and independent of the resume work. No code changes were needed.\n408: \n409: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n410: \n411: - Eight components still build their own `new ApiService(auth.getToken())`\n412:   (`dashboard/Inspiration`, `libraries/shared/Recommender`,\n413:   `calendars/ShareCalendarModal`, `settings/ExportSettings`,\n414:   `settings/TelegramBotConnection`, and the three\n415:   `settings/notifications/Manage*` components). They are outside TASK-1's\n416:   `state/*` scope, so they still snapshot the token and have no 401 handler and\n417:   can drift during a long-lived session. Worth converting to `auth.apiService` in\n418:   a follow-up.\n419: - `NavProfileEntry`'s `failed` flag resets only when `imagePath` changes, so a\n420:   transient image failure that later becomes loadable within the same session\n421:   (same path) still shows the letter fallback until navigation/reload.\n422: - Pre-existing repo-wide `prettier --check` drift and the unrelated\n423:   `StatisticWidget` component-test failure (both present before this job).\n\n(End of file - total 423 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nA permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\nstayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\nfeature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\nclosed and \"nothing happened\") and the in-memory user — including\n`profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\n`Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\n\nImplemented as a layered fix:\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/cover_reload-after-time-away/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: reload after time away\n\nid: cover\nstatus: open\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (via manigot)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nA permanently-open solyto tab drifted into a zombie state: `Auth.loggedIn`\nstayed `true` in memory while the stored token was expired/revoked, so every\nfeature request failed silently (`Notes.create()` returned `null`, the modal\nclosed and \"nothing happened\") and the in-memory user — including\n`profile.profile_image_path` — was never refreshed. A hard reload re-ran\n`Auth.load()` and fixed everything.\n\nImplemented as a layered fix:\n\n- **TASK-1** — all state stores now share `Auth`'s single `ApiService` instance\n  instead of snapshotting the token at construction, so a runtime refresh\n  reaches every request. Logout clears the token on that shared instance.\n- **TASK-2** — `Auth` re-validates the session when the app resumes\n  (`visibilitychange` → visible, `online`) and on a low-frequency interval while\n  visible: expired/near-expiry → single-flight `refresh()`, then\n  `loadAdditionalData()` to refresh the in-memory user; definitive refresh\n  rejection → logout.\n- **TASK-3** — `ApiService` runs a global 401 recovery ladder for non-auth\n  endpoints: adopt another tab's fresher persisted token, else single-flight\n  refresh, retry the original request exactly once; only a definitive refresh\n  rejection logs out. Auth endpoints and network errors never trigger recovery.\n- **TASK-4** — `Notes.create()` / `createCategory()` failures are surfaced via\n  `UiNotifications.error()` (translation-aware) instead of being swallowed, and\n  the modal + user input are kept so the entry can be retried.\n- **TASK-5** — the root layout reacts to a mid-session logout (`$effect` on\n  `auth.loggedIn`) and redirects to login/setup with a session-expired notice.\n- **TASK-6** — audit: keep the earlier profile-image fix; it covers a distinct\n  failure mode (transient/cross-origin image fetch) and is not made redundant\n  by the resume-driven `loadAdditionalData()`.\n- **TASK-7** — verification; see below.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1 — shared session ApiService\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `clear()` now calls\n  `apiService.updateAuthToken(null)` so no store keeps sending a revoked token.\n- `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` (33 stores) — `this.apiService = this.auth.apiService`\n  replacing `new ApiService(this.auth.getToken())`; `Finances`/`Todos` change\n  their constructor default parameter to `auth.apiService`.\n- `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`, `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts` —\n  updated to assert stores share the instance (and the mock auth exposes it).\n\nTASK-2 — resume-driven session validation\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `SESSION_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS` (hourly),\n  `startSessionMonitor()` registering `visibilitychange` + `online` (guarded by\n  `browser`), interval started while visible and stopped while hidden,\n  `validateSession()` doing the local `expires_at` comparison and only touching\n  the network when action is needed, then `loadAdditionalData()`. `refresh()` is\n  single-flight (`refreshInFlight`) and `performRefresh()` refreshes the shared\n  instance's token.\n\nTASK-3 — global 401 recovery\n- `src/lib/services/ApiService.ts` — `AUTH_ENDPOINTS` bypass list,\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler()`, `fetchWithRecovery()` (used by every request\n  method) which retries exactly once with the current token after a successful\n  recovery, and lets network errors propagate untouched. `updateAuthToken` now\n  accepts `null`.\n- `src/lib/state/Auth.svelte.ts` — `recoverFromUnauthorized()` /\n  `performRecovery()` (single-flight) ladder: (a) `adoptExternalSession()` reads\n  the persisted auth (multi-tab adoption), (b) `refresh()`, (c) logout only on a\n  definitive refresh rejection.\n- `tests/unit/services/ApiService.test.ts` — new \"401 recovery\" cases: retry\n  once with the fresh token, no retry when recovery declines, no recovery for\n  auth endpoints, no recovery on network error.\n- `tests/unit/auth/Auth.test.ts` — mock ApiService exposes\n  `setUnauthorizedHandler`.\n\nTASK-4 — surface failed note mutations\n- `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts` — `ts`/`notifications` context fields;\n  `create()` and `createCategory()` call `notifications.error()` on failure and\n  keep `inputValue`/`createParent`/`modalOpen`; the modal is closed by the store\n  on success instead of optimistically by the caller.\n- `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte` — removed the optimistic `notes.closeModal()`\n  before create/confirm so a failed attempt leaves the modal (and the user's\n  input) open. (Needed to fulfil \"keep the input in the modal\"; the store now\n  owns success-close, which also handles the edit path whose return value is\n  `null`.)\n- `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts` + `src/lib/types/translation.ts` —\n  `notes.create_error`, `notes.create_folder_error`, `auth.session_expired`.\n- `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` — stubs `getTranslation`/`getUiNotifications`,\n  asserts the error notification and that input/modal are retained on failure.\n\nTASK-5 — reactive mid-session logout\n- `src/routes/+layout.svelte` — imports `getUiNotifications`; `$effect` tracks\n  `auth.loggedIn`: on a logged-in → logged-out transition on a protected route it\n  shows `auth.session_expired` and redirects to login/setup. Auth/setup routes\n  and manual logout (`/auth/logout`) are excluded, so no redirect loop.\n\nTASK-6 — profile-image audit (no code change)\n- Keep `src/service-worker.ts` same-origin GET guard and\n  `src/lib/components/ui/NavProfileEntry.svelte` retry-on-error + letter\n  fallback. Rationale: the resume work fixes *stale data* (an expired token\n  hiding a newer `profile_image_path`), while the earlier fix addresses a\n  *broken in-session image fetch* — the SW previously answered the cross-origin\n  `<img>` with a synthetic `503`, and `<img>` never retries, so no amount of\n  resume-time `loadAdditionalData()` recovers it. `loadAdditionalData()` (boot /\n  login / resume) and `profileCache` (other users' public profiles for\n  `getPublicProfile`) remain independently necessary. Both fixes are\n  complementary; nothing was removed.\n\n## Verification (TASK-7)\n\nCommands (this worktree, node 22):\n\n- `npm run check` — **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n- `npm test` — 53/54 files pass, **715 tests pass**. One unrelated pre-existing\n  failure: `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\n  requested color classes`, which expects `.bg-blue-50`/`.text-blue-600` while\n  the unchanged component uses theme classes (`bg-c-btn/10`, `text-c-btn`).\n  Neither the component nor the test is touched by this job.\n- `npm run lint` — no **new** ESLint errors are introduced. ESLint reports 13\n  errors across the one-line-touched store files (`Calendars`, `Contacts`,\n  `DevRequests`, `LinkLibrary`, `MovieLibrary`, `QuickAdd`, `QuoteLibrary`,\n  `RecipeLibrary`, `UserNotifications`), but every one of them is on a line the\n  job does not touch and reproduces identically on the base commit (`22c5a68`,\n  verified via `eslint --stdin`). The files carrying the actual logic changes\n  (`ApiService.ts`, `Auth.svelte.ts`, `Notes.svelte.ts`, `+layout.svelte`, and\n  the tests) are clean. `prettier --check` fails repo-wide (402 files) including\n  files untouched by this job (and even `HEAD` versions of unchanged files), i.e.\n  pre-existing drift with the installed prettier 3.6.2 + tailwind plugin; not\n  introduced here.\n- Backend probes: **not possible in this environment** — no dev API is running\n  (`http://localhost:8000` refused). The two open backend facts (does `POST\n  /auth/refresh` accept an already-expired token? is the old token revoked on\n  rotation?) therefore remain unverified; the implementation is deliberately\n  agnostic (recovery ladder), so both answers are handled.\n- Re-verified in a follow-up pass (same worktree, node 22) — results unchanged\n  and no code edits were needed: `npm run check` 0 errors / 0 warnings;\n  `npm test` 715 passed with the same single unrelated pre-existing failure\n  (`tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget`, a file graph this\n  job does not touch); `npx eslint` clean on every changed source file. Also\n  confirmed on the branch that TASK-6's audit is accurate: the service worker's\n  same-origin GET guard (`src/service-worker.ts`) and `NavProfileEntry`'s\n  retry-then-letter fallback are both present and independent of the resume\n  work.\n- Independently re-verified once more (node 22): `npm run check` → 0 errors /\n  0 warnings; `npm test` → 715 passed with the same single unrelated\n  `StatisticWidget` component-test failure; ES